{"id": "79", "question": "how to cook brats", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief guide on how to cook brats:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Combine beer, onions, red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper in a large pot. Bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\n5. Reduce heat to medium and cook for 10 to 12 minutes.\n6. Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and place them on the preheated grill.\n7. Cook the bratwurst for 5 to 10 minutes, turning once.\n8. Serve the bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\n\nSo, to cook brats, you first prepare the grill, then cook the bratwurst in a beer mixture before grilling them until they're done.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the type of bratwurst mentioned in the passage.\nLook for any specific cooking instructions or methods mentioned in the passage for the type of bratwurst identified.\nLook for any specific cooking methods or seasoning recommendations for the identified type of bratwurst in the passage.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 59.482, "generation_time_seconds": 26.5483, "selection_time_seconds": 32.9333, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [4418, 1526, 279, 2661, 46769, 311, 10542, 894, 3151, 11221, 476, 5413, 369, 17233, 1411, 1862, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.2886, -1.1726, -0.0027, -0.4682, -0.056, -0.1126, -0.8102, -0.1232, -0.8754, -0.4425, -0.0753, -0.1993, -0.0505, -0.0003, -0.0023, -0.0005, -0.0133, -0.7973], "cumulative_logprob": -8.4908, "norm_logp": -0.4717, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 18}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 13966, 9733, 304, 279, 46