{"id": "90", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so that it runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n4. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n5. Repeat step 4 to make two smears.\n6. Allow the smears to air dry.\n7. Label the slides clearly.\n8. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\n\nNote: It is important to sterilize the needle used to obtain the blood sample by heating it with a flame before using it. Additionally, it is essential to wear rubber gloves when handling blood to avoid coming into contact with potentially infectious materials.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the given passages for specific instructions or guidelines on preparing a blood slide. Look for details such as the materials needed, the steps involved, any precautions, and expected outcomes.\nLook for any diagrams, tables, or other visual aids that might illustrate the steps involved in preparing a blood slide.\nLook for any references to specific techniques or methods mentioned in the passages that could be used for preparing a blood slide.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 58.0, "generation_time_seconds": 34.7499, "selection_time_seconds": 23.2499, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 3405, 25, 330, 5158, 311, 10549, 6543, 14983, 1, 323, 10542, 279, 1376, 5424, 481, 20045, 11, 6543, 14983, 13