{"id": "101", "question": "how to sync audiobook from iphone to itunes", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to sync audiobooks from an iPhone to iTunes:\n\n1. Turn on the Manually manage music setting in iTunes.\n2. Download the audiobook you want from iTunes.\n3. Connect your iPhone to the computer via USB cable.\n4. Click on \"Audiobooks\" on the left task pane of the iTunes window.\n5. Select the audiobook you want to sync by clicking on its title.\n6. Click \"Sync Audiobooks\" and choose the audiobooks you want to transfer.\n7. Click \"Apply\" to start the syncing process.\n\nAlternatively, you can use Syncios Audiobook Transfer to transfer audiobooks from your iPhone to iTunes. The software allows two-way transfer of files, so you can not only backup files to your PC but also transfer audiobooks from your PC to your iPhone. Here are the steps to use Syncios Audiobook Transfer:\n\n1. Launch Syncios Audiobook Transfer on your computer.\n2. Connect your iPhone to the computer via USB cable.\n3. Click on \"Audiobooks\" on the top menu bar.\n4. Select the audiobooks you want to transfer and click \"Export\" to save them to your computer.\n5. Alternatively, you can also click \"Import\" to add new audiobooks from your computer to your iPhone.\n6. Click \"Apply\" to start the transfer process.\n\nNote that the above steps are based on the assumption that you have already turned on the Manually manage music setting in iTunes. If you have not done so, you will need to do so before attempting to sync your audiobooks.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nRead the passage and gather relevant information.\nIdentify the key components or steps mentioned in the passage related to syncing an audiobook from iPhone to iTunes.\nBased on the given passage, it does not contain specific information about how to sync an audiobook from an iPhone to iTunes. The passage focuses on the functionality of an audiobook on an iPhone, including the ability to shuffle and play it, but does not provide any instructions on the syncing process.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 42.332, "generation_time_seconds": 25.8465, "selection_time_seconds": 16.4859, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [10380, 369, 894, 3151, 11221, 476, 5413, 3897, 304, 279, 2661, 46769, 389, 96145, 46368, 674, 14685, 504, 458, 12167, 311, 13025, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.0003, -0.0126, -1.2238, -0.6456, -0.0481, -0.018, -1.8144, -1.1513, -0.018, -0.0, -0.6468, -0.0412, -1.4126, -1.2427, -0.0669, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0016, -0.0358, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0118, -0.0727], "cumulative_logprob": -11.4642, "norm_logp": -0.4777, "input_len": 142, "output_tokens": 24}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.1967, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0083, -0.0001], "cumulative_logprob": -2.2057, "norm_logp": -0.2451, "input_len": 142, "output_tokens": 9}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3772, 315, 279, 21085, 429, 5610, 1995, 911, 96145, 46368, 674, 14685, 504, 458, 12167, 311, 13025, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.0181, -0.0019, -0.0526, -4.2293, -0.1391, -0.0006, -0.0245, -0.0125, -5.7465, -0.8591, -0.4732, -0.0328, -0.0123, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0099, -0.1246, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0073, -0.0569], "cumulative_logprob": -13.8014, "norm_logp": -0.6273, "input_len": 142, "output_tokens": 22}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [4418, 279, 21085, 323, 9567, 9760, 1995, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-4.6967, -0.4654, -2.217, -2.223, -6.6891, -0.8634, -0.0474, -2.4184, -0.0492], "cumulative_logprob": -19.6696, "norm_logp": -2.1855, "input_len": 142, "output_tokens": 9}, {"phase": "vote