{"id": "109", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the Windward Islands are located in the southeastern part of the Caribbean Sea and are exposed to the wind (\"windward\") of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies), while the Leeward Islands are located in the northwestern part of the Lesser Antilles and are away from the wind (\"lee\"). The main difference between them is their exposure to the wind and the resulting climate. The Windward Islands get more rain and are wetter due to their exposure to the wind, while the Leeward Islands are drier but still get rain.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nTo answer: Identify and compare the physical characteristics of the Leeward and Windward islands.\nDetermine the geographical location and direction of the islands relative to the prevailing winds.\nIdentify the specific physical features that define the Leeward and Windward islands, such as their mountainous versus flat terrain, and their orientation relative to the prevailing winds.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 46.116, "generation_time_seconds": 29.1418, "selection_time_seconds": 16.9739, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 4226, 279, 3405, 911, 279, 6672, 1948, 279, 1967, 24035, 323, 22087, 1606, 29000, 11, 582, 1184, 311, 23643, 279, 52901, 323, 11076, 774, 11799, 1948, 1493, 1378, 13604, 315, 279, 34274, 13, 6771, 594, 1438, 1495, 279, 32711, 7354, 1447], "logp_list": [-2.6385, -0.663, -0.1613, -0.001, -0.7085, -0.0002, -0.008, 0.0, -0.0041, -1.366, -0.0, -0.0164, -0.0036, 0.0, -0.3985, -0.0057, -0.7475, -0.0555, -0.0028, -1.7384, -0.0604, -1.8224, -0.0848, -0.2402, -0.0279, -1.778, -0.2147