{"id": "139", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded. The block concept is followed, where assets of the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are grouped together and considered as a single asset. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, even if it is not used for business or profession in that year and subsequent years.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe question asks about the treatment of an asset that is discarded under the Income Tax Act. To answer this, we need to analyze the given passages for specific information on how assets are handled in terms of taxation, particularly when they are discarded.\nGiven the instruction, the next logical reasoning step is to identify specific information within the provided passages that relates to the treatment of assets when they are discarded. This involves looking for clauses, definitions, or examples that discuss the taxation of disposed assets, as this is the core focus of the question.\nIdentify any specific clauses or sections in the Income Tax Act that deal with the disposal of assets. Look for definitions, examples, or procedural steps that indicate how assets should be treated for tax purposes upon discard.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 71.238, "generation_time_seconds": 45.2476, "selection_time_seconds": 25.9908, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [785, 3405, 17064, 911, 279, 6380, 315, 458, 9329, 429, 374, 43210, 1212, 279