{"id": "159", "question": "how to factory reset a htc one vx", "gt": "To factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Switch off the device by holding down the Power button for a while.\n2. Press and hold the Volume Down + Power key for a couple of seconds until Bootloader Mode menu appears on the screen.\n3. From the menu, choose \"Factory Data Reset\" by using Volume buttons to scroll and Power key to select.\n4. Confirm the reset by pressing \"Erase Everything\".\n5. Release all keys when the process is complete.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nTo factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\nPlease provide the steps to factory reset an HTC One VX.\nTo factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 38.792, "generation_time_seconds": 25.793, "selection_time_seconds": 12.9987, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.2229, 0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0006, -0.0, -0.0049, -0.0], "cumulative_logprob": -2.2286, "norm_logp": -0.2476, "input_len": 141, "output_tokens": 9}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [2082, 55856, 279, 3897, 21085, 311, 1477, 279, 7354, 311, 8633, 7585, 458, 48267, 3776, 78177, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-5.7051, -0.0001, -0.0398, -1.5312, -1.0533, -1.1325, -0.8833, -2.9165, -1.2152, -3.0469, -0.0828, -0.0, -0.1112, -0.0, -0.0161, -0.0084, -0.0306, -0.0897], "cumulative_logprob": -17.8627, "norm_logp": -0.9924, "input_len": 141, "output_tokens": 18}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [40, 1184, 311, 1349, 1995, 911, 279, 48267, 3776, 78177, 323, 1181, 8633, 7585, 1882, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.5622, -1.5097, -0.7148, -5