{"id": "214", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "To properly wash wine glasses, you should scrub them by hand as it's the safest cleaning method. First, lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. If hot water and mild detergent can’t get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the passages for any specific instructions or recommendations regarding the washing of wine glasses.\nLook for details about the best way to clean wine glasses, such as using specific detergents or avoiding certain cleaning methods.\nIdentify any specific tools or techniques mentioned for washing wine glasses, such as using a soft cloth or avoiding abrasive scrubbers.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 49.402, "generation_time_seconds": 28.9357, "selection_time_seconds": 20.4665, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 7236, 323, 6813, 315, 279, 13078, 28147, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.5685, -0.0028, -0.0427, -1.1113, -1.0102, -1.0836, -0.0045, -0.598, -0.001, -0.0559, -0.847, -0.0084], "cumulat