{"id": "244", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "The FEHA (Fair Employment and Housing Act) and the ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) have several differences. The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Another important difference is the requirement of disability. The ADA requires a physical or mental impairment to substantially limit a major life activity, while the FEHA only requires that a mental and physical disability limit a major life activity, without the need for it to be a substantial limit.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the specific details provided about feha and ada to identify key differences. Look for contrasts in their characteristics, functions, or applications. Identify any distinct features or attributes that distinguish feha from ada.\nExamine any examples or comparisons given in the passage to understand how feha and ada are used or applied in different contexts. This will help identify their practical differences.\nReview the information provided in the passage to ensure that all relevant aspects of feha and ada have been considered. This may include checking for any additional context or background information that could affect the comparison.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 58.704, "generation_time_seconds": 35.3569, "selection_time_seconds": 23.3471, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 1376, 17452, 323, 17473, 315, 1152, 4223, 323, 34234, 304, 279, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.503, -0.0009, -0.1412, -0.5257, -1.4604, -2.1773, -1.9038, -0.012