{"id": "286", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "gt": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 325-350 degrees Fahrenheit. If you don't have time to defrost the roast, put it in the oven at 250 F for about an hour. Afterwards, take it out and season it with salt, pepper, and any seasonings you prefer, such as thyme, oregano or garlic. Rub the surface with 2 tsp. of olive oil. Place the roast in a roasting pan with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards, and put it back in the oven for about 1.5 to 3 hours depending on its size, or about 20-30 minutes per pound. Make sure the roast is cooked thoroughly by using a meat thermometer; the internal temperature should reach 150 degrees Fahrenheit. Once it is cooked, cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the recipe instructions and any additional cooking tips provided in the passages.\nIdentify the specific cooking method and temperature settings mentioned for the oven cooking of the frozen pork loin roast.\nLook for any specific cooking times or duration mentioned in the passages for the oven cooking of the frozen pork loin roast.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 52.095, "generation_time_seconds": 25.8714, "selection_time_seconds": 26.2234, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 11116, 11221, 323, 894, 5107, 17233, 10414, 3897, 304, 279, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.3281, -0.0115, -0.0178, -2.1765, -0.7617, -4.662, -2.5276, -1.3843, -0.9016, -0.07, -0.0905, -0.0638, -0.0, -0.1496, -0.6201, -0.4904], "cumulative_logprob": -15.2555, "norm_logp": -0.9535, "input_len":