{"id": "354", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, I can confidently answer the following questions:\n\nWhat is company goodwill?\nCompany goodwill refers to the positive image and reputation of a business that is built over time through providing quality products or services, satisfying customers, and building strong relationships with them. Goodwill is a valuable asset for any business as it helps to attract new customers, retain existing ones, and attract investors.\n\nWhy is goodwill important in business?\nGoodwill is important in business because it helps to build trust and loyalty among customers, which leads to long-term relationships and repeat business. A strong reputation and goodwill can also make a business more attractive to potential investors and buyers. Additionally, goodwill can help a business to stand out from its competitors and establish a unique identity in the marketplace.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the key concepts related to company goodwill mentioned in the given passages.\nExamine the context and relationships between these concepts as explained in the passages, and determine their interconnections and implications for understanding company goodwill.\nExamine the specific examples provided in the passages to illustrate the concept of company goodwill and its importance.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 46.583, "generation_time_seconds": 27.1535, "selection_time_seconds": 19.4292, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 1376, 6813, 315, 2813, 81646, 9733, 304, 279, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.533, -0.0028, -0.1429, -1.1753, -1.2041, -0.0811, -0.2415, -0.000