{"id": "412", "question": "how do i breed a shugabeats in my singing monsters", "gt": "To breed a Shugabeats in My Singing Monsters, you must first obtain the Shugabush Monster from another island. This will turn your Shugabush Monsters into an egg. After hatching them, buy the breeding structure. Then, use the Shugabush and the Furcorn in the Shugabush Island breeding structure to get the Shugabeats monster. The order of the monsters does not matter.", "pred": "To breed a Shugabeat in your Singing Monsters, you need to have a Shugabeat egg. These eggs can be obtained by defeating certain Shugabeat-related battles or through in-game events. To use the egg, you should navigate to the breeding section of your game, select the Shugabeat egg, and wait for the game to process the breeding. The breeding process may take a varying amount of time depending on the game's settings and your in-game resources.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: To breed a Shugabeat in your Singing Monsters, you need to have a Shugabeat egg. These eggs can be obtained by defeating certain Shugabeat-related battles or through in-game events. To use the egg, you should navigate to the breeding section of your game, select the Shugabeat egg, and wait for the game to process the breeding. The breeding process may take a varying amount of time depending on the game's settings and your in-game resources.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nTo breed a Shugabeat in your Singing Monsters, you need to follow the specific breeding rules set by the game. Usually, you would need to have a Shugabeat egg. These eggs can be obtained by defeating certain Shugabeat-related battles or through in-game events. To use the egg, you should navigate to the breeding section of your game, select the Shugabeat egg, and wait for the game to process the breeding. The breeding process may take a varying amount of time depending on the game's settings and your in-game resources.\nAnswer: To breed a Shugabeat in your Singing Monsters, you need to have a Shugabeat egg. These eggs can be obtained by defeating certain Shugabeat-related battles or through in-game events. To use the egg, you should navigate to the breeding section of your game, select the Shugabeat egg, and wait for the game to process the breeding. The breeding process may take a varying amount of time depending on the game's settings and your in-game resources.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nAnswer: To breed a Shugabeat in your Singing Monsters, you need to have a Shugabeat egg. These eggs can be obtained by defeating certain Shugabeat-related battles or through in-game events. To use the egg, you should navigate to the breeding section of your game, select the Shugabeat egg, and wait for the game to process the breeding. The breeding process may take a varying amount of time depending on the game's settings and your in-game resources.", "time_sec": 56.406, "generation_time_seconds": 41.3233, "selection_time_seconds": 15.0822, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 27775, 264, 1417, 768, 8229, 266, 304, 697, 10833, 287, 62708, 11, 498, 1184, 311, 1795, 279, 3151, 39208, 5601, 738, 553, 279, 1809, 13, 32967, 11, 498, 1035, 1184, 311, 614, 264, 1417, 768, 8229, 266, 18636, 13, 4220, 18805, 646, 387, 12180, 553, 53116, 3654, 1417, 768, 8229, 266, 13904, 24554, 476, 1526, 304, 19395, 4357, 13, 2014, 990, 279, 18636, 11, 498, 1265, 20876, 311, 279, 39208, 3772, 315, 697, 1809, 11, 3293, 279, 1417, 768, 8229, 266, 18636, 11, 323, 3783, 369, 279, 1809, 311, 1882, 279, 39208, 13, 576, 39208, 1882, 1231, 1896, 264, 28765, 3311, 315, 882, 11649, 389, 279, 1809, 594, 5003, 323, 697, 304, 19395, 4963, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.2942, -0.5297, -0.0013, -0.0341, -0.0041, -0.0164, -1.9424, -0.0049, -1.2768, -0.1205, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.2546, -0.0747, -0.3881, -0.0022, -0.8725, -1.7639, -1.6042, -0.0