{"id": "480", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"change of address u.s. postal service\":\n\nTo change your address with the U.S. Postal Service, you can visit the USPS website (moversguide.usps.com), call the USPS Call Center (1-800-ASK-USPS), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office. You can also use the USPS change of address feature to notify up to 100 organizations, including the Postal Service, with secure encryption technology to protect your data.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe question asks about changing an address with the U.S. Postal Service. This is a straightforward request that does not require analysis of any physical details or logical reasoning steps. It is a simple procedural question that can be addressed with basic knowledge about postal service procedures.\nThe question asks about changing an address with the U.S. Postal Service. This is a straightforward request that does not require analysis of any physical details or logical reasoning steps. It is a simple procedural question that can be addressed with basic knowledge about postal service procedures.\nThe physical details are presented in the form of a question. The question is straightforward and does not require analysis of any physical details or logical reasoning steps. It is a simple procedural question that can be addressed with basic knowledge about postal service procedures.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 57.326, "generation_time_seconds": 33.7376, "selection_time_seconds": 23.5884, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [785, 3405, 17064, 911, 10018, 279, 2621, 448, 279, 547,