{"id": "648", "question": "color of urin meaning", "gt": "The color of urine can indicate various health conditions. Normal urine is typically pale yellow, due to the pigment urochrome. If kidney diseases are present, the filtration and re-absorption stages of urine production may be malfunctioning, altering this pale color. Red urine is typically a sign of blood in the urine, which can indicate serious conditions like infections or cancer. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. Foods and medications can also affect urine color, with beets, berries, and fava beans being among the most likely to cause changes.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the relevant information from the given passages regarding the color of urine.\nLook for any specific descriptions of urine color and its potential meanings or implications.\nLook for any specific descriptions of urine color and its potential meanings or implications.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 48.619, "generation_time_seconds": 23.9022, "selection_time_seconds": 24.7171, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 9760, 1995, 504, 279, 2661, 46769, 8826, 279, 1894, 315, 39235, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.439, -0.0033, -0.1021, -1.4411, -0.1535, -1.5923, -0.0, -1.2097, -0.296, -1.9681, -0.0684, -0.0925, -0.0009, -0.0034, -2.7465, -0.0208], "cumulative_logprob": -12.1376, "norm_logp": -0.7586, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 16}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [10380, 369, 894, 6286, 315, 4335, 977, 7987, 476, 279, 7966, 4815, 3654, 7987, 304, 279, 3897, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-4.939, -0.1303, -0.4954, -0.8051, -0.011