{"id": "722", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to poach an egg using a PoachPod®:\n\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Crack an egg into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk.\n3. Gently slide the pod into the boiling water, making sure it stays upright and no water gets in.\n4. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for 6 minutes.\n5. Use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and press the bottom to release the poached egg.\n\nSo, to summarize, the steps to poach an egg using a PoachPod® are:\n\n1. Bring water to a boil.\n2. Crack egg into pod.\n3. Float pod in boiling water.\n4. Cook for 6 minutes.\n5. Remove pod from water.\n6. Release egg onto plate.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the specific instruction or detail about using a poachpod from the given passages.\nExamine the steps or guidelines provided in the passages for using a poachpod to poach an egg.\nSummarize and condense the key steps or guidelines from the passages for poaching an egg using a poachpod.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 58.114, "generation_time_seconds": 24.6476, "selection_time_seconds": 33.4666, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3151, 7600, 476, 7716, 911, 1667, 264, 3193, 610, 39073, 504, 279, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.3143, -0.0016, -0.0102, -0.6107, -8.7086, -0.217, -3.3475, -0.7999, -0.5523, -0.0233, -0.0153, -0.0001, -0.002, -2.0351, -0.0006, -0.6466, -0.4116, -0.079, -0.003], "cumulative_logprob": -19.7787, "norm_logp": -1.041, "input_len": 143, "output_tokens": 19}, 