{"id": "38", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to cook pollock:\n\nPreheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper or aluminum foil. You can also add sliced onions, green peppers, and tomatoes on top of the fillets. Bake for 15 minutes or until the fish flakes easily with a fork. If desired, top with cheese and return to the oven for an additional 3 minutes or until the cheese is melted.\n\nTherefore, the answer is not \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nLook for any cooking instructions or recipes related to pollock in the given passages.\nLook for any references to specific cooking methods, ingredients, or seasoning suggestions for pollock in the given passages.\nLook for any details about the preparation or handling of pollock before cooking, such as cleaning or cutting instructions in the given passages.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 51.109, "generation_time_seconds": 30.426, "selection_time_seconds": 20.6827, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [2082, 55856, 279, 4650, 17233, 5413, 323, 17975, 12538, 369, 17233, 1471, 1023, 429, 525, 16626, 1483, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.7376, -0.0, -0.0272, -6.7565, -0.1015, -0.003, -1.7337, -1.355, -0.2165, -0.3354, -3.6892, -0.0126, -0.0, -4.3333, -0.2498, -0.8484, -0.445, -0.4924, -0.0435], "cumulative_logprob": -24.3806, "norm_logp": -1.2832, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 19}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 421, 279, 21085, 33845, 894, 3151, 17233, 5413, 476, 17975, 7354, 369, 1471, 1023, 3118, 389, 27