{"id": "48", "question": "how to fold a quilt", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to fold a quilt:\n\n1. Lay the quilt on a flat surface.\n2. Fold the lower right corner up towards the center of the quilt, ensuring the fold is on the bias.\n3. Fold the lower left corner up towards the center of the quilt, also on the bias.\n4. Fold the top left corner down towards the center of the quilt, again on the bias.\n5. Fold the top right corner down towards the center of the quilt, again on the bias.\n\nThese steps will result in a neatly folded quilt with four even corners. Note that the size of the quilt is not specified in the passages, so these steps can be applied to quilts of any size.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nTo determine how to fold a quilt, the first step is to identify the size and shape of the quilt and the desired folding method. Typically, quilts come in rectangular or square shapes, and common folding methods include folding the quilt in half, quartering it, or folding it into smaller sections for storage.\nThe next logical step in the reasoning process would be to describe the folding method in detail. This would include explaining the specific actions needed to achieve the desired folding, such as folding the quilt in half lengthwise, then folding it in half again widthwise to create quarters.\nThe final step in the reasoning process would be to provide a clear and concise conclusion on how to fold a quilt. This would involve summarizing the folding method and offering any additional tips or considerations for successful folding.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 68.509, "generation_time_seconds": 44.9916, "selection_time_seconds": 23.517, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rol