{"id": "140", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that when an asset is discarded by a business but not sold, the Income Tax Act allows the scrap value of the asset to be deducted from the opening work-in-progress (WDV) of such asset in the previous year in which it was discarded. This reduction is taken into account while computing the depreciation expense for the subsequent years. However, any changes made to the value of the block must be made strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of Income Tax Act 1961.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the specific section or provision of the Income Tax Act that addresses the treatment of assets when they are discarded. Review the relevant sections for any specific instructions on accounting for such assets.\nLook for any specific mention of asset disposal, discarding, or write-off in the Income Tax Act. Identify any instructions on how to account for these actions, including any tax implications or reporting requirements.\nLook for any specific mention of asset disposal, discarding, or write-off in the Income Tax Act. Identify any instructions on how to account for these actions, including any tax implications or reporting requirements.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 53.138, "generation_time_seconds": 35.7588, "selection_time_seconds": 17.379, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 3151, 14158, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 429, 28143, 311, 279, 6380, 315, 11770, 979, 807, 525, 43210, 13, 4248, 369, 19156, 14550, 448, 279, 33445, 315, 11770, 323, 862, 3742, 24154, 382], "logp_list": [-2.21