{"id": "179", "question": "how to change the sleep time on my computer", "gt": "Sure, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to change the sleep time on my computer\" based on the given passages:\n\nTo change the sleep time on your computer, follow these steps:\n\n1. Click the Start menu and select Control Panel.\n2. In the Control Panel, click on Power Options.\n3. In the Power Options window, click on \"Change when the computer sleeps\" on the left side of the window.\n4. In the \"Put the computer to sleep\" section, change the duration of time to the desired amount of time you want the computer to sit idle before it goes to sleep.\n5. Alternatively, you can also toggle off the option to enter Sleep mode automatically.\n\nIf you are using Windows 10, you can also search for \"Power Options\" in the taskbar search box and select it to open the Power Options window.\n\nIf you are using Windows 8.1 / Windows RT 8.1, you can move your mouse to the lower left-hand corner of the screen, right-click the Start button, and select Shut down or sign out, and then select Shut down.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the specific system or operating environment of the computer (e.g., Windows, macOS, Linux).\nFind the specific settings related to sleep or screen timeout on the computer's operating system.\nLook for the 'sleep' or 'power options' settings in the system control panel or settings menu.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 65.181, "generation_time_seconds": 30.272, "selection_time_seconds": 34.909, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [10380, 369, 279, 6366, 594, 5003, 5022, 11, 11136, 24758, 1526, 279, 1191, 5022, 476, 1849, 5003, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.2408, -0.02