{"id": "256", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "To clean your dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Remove the outside cover on the vent.\n2. Use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe.\n3. If possible, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there as well.\n4. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter and clean it thoroughly.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the type of dryer vent: Determine whether the dryer vent is flexible or rigid. This will determine the cleaning method needed.\nDetermine the current state of the dryer vent: Check for any visible debris, lint accumulation, or signs of wear and tear.\nGather appropriate cleaning tools: Depending on the type of dryer vent and the state of the vent, you may need a vacuum cleaner, a dryer vent brush, or a flexible snake.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 48.432, "generation_time_seconds": 30.8139, "selection_time_seconds": 17.6177, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.9455, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0042, -0.0], "cumulative_logprob": -3.9502, "norm_logp": -0.4389, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 9}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3151, 6813, 315, 264, 46622, 10378, 429, 1184, 15826, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.2669, -0.0023, -0.0592, -1.852, -3.5926, -0.0989, -0.6933, -0.0006, -0.0006, -0.0733, -0.086, -0.0674, -0.1657, -0.0059], "cumulative_logprob": -7.9647, "norm_logp": -0.5689, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 14}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_i