{"id": "342", "question": "when you have a bowel movement do you lose weight", "gt": "While you may technically lose a small amount of weight after a bowel movement, this does not come from a loss of body fat. The decrease in body weight does not come from fat loss in stools, but rather from the elimination of undigested food and waste. Weight loss is primarily tied to your caloric intake and expenditure, not bowel movements. Unless your scale is highly accurate, you're unlikely to notice a difference in your body weight before and after a bowel movement.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the relevant information about the relationship between bowel movements and weight loss in the given passage.\nConclude whether the passage supports the idea that bowel movements cause weight loss or not.\nIdentify the specific mechanisms or processes described in the passage that relate to weight loss and bowel movements.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 44.446, "generation_time_seconds": 28.1969, "selection_time_seconds": 16.2491, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [22524, 1495, 279, 3405, 1119, 6813, 25, 715, 16, 13, 3555, 374, 264, 65258, 7203, 5267, 17, 13, 3555, 11137, 264, 65258, 7203, 5267, 18, 13, 2585, 1558, 264, 65258, 7203, 7802, 4680, 5267, 19, 13, 12553, 264, 65258, 7203, 5240, 4680, 4709, 1939], "logp_list": [-6.8146, -0.0717, -0.0041, -0.1257, -0.7127, -1.3102, -0.3285, -1.1864, -0.0478, -0.0047, -1.1848, -0.2501, -0.0703, -0.0021, -0.0, -0.1323, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.4765, -3.9524, -1.5318, -0.1784, -0.0, -0.012, -0.0, -0.0, -0.809, -0.1975, -0.166, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.4597, -0.6738, -1.1132, -0.0044, -0.0, -2.1238, -0.503, -0.0039, -0.0, -2.8607, -0.036, -0.0005, -1.2783], "c