{"id": "356", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive feelings and loyalty of customers towards a business, gained through providing good services or products, building trust, and creating a strong reputation. Goodwill is important because it can increase customer retention, attract new customers, and make the business more attractive to investors and potential buyers.\n\nAccording to passage 3, goodwill is an intangible asset that represents the value of a business's reputation and customer connections, which can make the connection between the business and its customers permanent.\n\nTherefore, goodwill is important for businesses because it can lead to increased customer loyalty, positive word-of-mouth advertising, and higher sales, ultimately contributing to the long-term success and growth of the business.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nBased on the given question, the next logical reasoning step would be to identify the key terms and concepts related to \"company goodwill\" and \"why it is important.\" This involves breaking down the question into its core components to understand what is being asked about company goodwill and why it holds significance.\nThe next logical reasoning step would be to look for definitions or explanations of \"company goodwill\" within the given passages to establish what it refers to and why it is important. This involves identifying relevant sections where these concepts are discussed and extracting any supporting details or examples provided in the text.\nThe next logical reasoning step would be to analyze the given passages to find descriptions or explanations of what constitutes \"company goodwill\" and why it is important. This involves identifying relevant sections and extracting any supporting details or examples provided in the text regarding the nature of goodwill and its significance to companies.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 53.782, "generation_time_seconds": 37.2612, "selection_time_seconds": 16.5211, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [98969, 1437, 279, 2266, 315, 279, 3405, 553, 26312, 1128, 2813, 81646, 374, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-5.7741, -0.0013, -0.3635, -3.0113, -0.8059, -0.3348, -0.2887, -0.5889, -0.8911, -0.1761, -0.8906, -0.0002, -0.1275, -0.5077, -0.0087], "cumulative_logprob": -13.7704, "norm_logp": -0.918, "input_len": 139, "output_tokens": 15}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.6759, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0085, -0.0001], "cumulative_logprob": -3.6855, "norm_logp": -0.4095, "input_len": 139, "output_tokens": 9}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 3405, 11, 279, 1790, 19819, 32711, 3019, 1035, 387, 311, 10542, 279, 1376, 3793, 323, 18940, 5435, 311, 330, 10139, 81646, 1, 323, 330, 34634, 432, 374, 2989, 1189, 1096, 17601, 14719, 1495, 279, 3405, 1119, 1181, 6200, 6813, 311, 3535, 1128, 374, 1660, 4588, 911, 2813, 81646, 323, 3170, 432, 9982, 25361, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.408, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.5288, -0.1974, -0.4675, -0.3389, -0.4776, -0.004, -0.2149, -0.0, -0.8102, -0.0034, -0.0667, -1.6974, -0.346, -0.5251, -1.7546, -0.5048, -0.0473, -0.6872, -0.0, -0.4959, -0.0578, -0.0, -0.0761, -0.235, -0.7152, -0.3638, -0.345, -0.0936, -0.0, -0.2526, -0.284, -0.276, -1.2526, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0433, -0.0694, -0.3125, -0.5215, -0.1556, -1.4088, -0.9744, -0.2201, -1.6453, -0.0015, -0.0064, -4.1958, -0.5383, -0.0, -0.017, -3.1308, -0.0669, -0.7338, -0.007, -0.111, -0.0611], "cumulative_logprob": -30.7498, "norm_logp": -0.5212, "input_len": 139, 