{"id": "428", "question": "how do twins happen", "gt": "Twins are two offspring produced by the same pregnancy. They can be either monozygotic (identical), meaning they develop from one zygote that splits and forms two embryos, or dizygotic (fraternal), meaning they develop from two different eggs with each being fertilized by its own sperm cell. Monoamniotic twins occur when the split takes place after the ninth day after fertilization. Conjoined twins occur when the division of the developing zygote into 2 embryos occurs within 8 days of fertilization. Dizygotic twin pregnancies are more likely in women of West African descent, especially Yoruba, aged between 30 and 40 years, of above average height and weight, and who have had several previous pregnancies.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the key elements of the question, such as the types of twins and the mechanisms involved in their occurrence, and then look for relevant information in the provided passages.\nSearch for descriptions of genetic and biological processes related to twinning in the provided passages.\nAnalyze the mechanisms of twinning as described in the passages.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 50.706, "generation_time_seconds": 25.5801, "selection_time_seconds": 25.126, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 2661, 21085, 323, 10542, 894, 1995, 476, 10295, 429, 10339, 1246, 43636, 3537, 13, 9192, 369, 3565, 911, 23275, 11364, 11, 55004, 11, 476, 1008, 9363, 6398, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.5806, -0.215, -0.026, -2.5662, -1.3729, -4.4436, -0.1276, -0.4017, -0.8357, -4.1752, -0.3833, -1.7578, -0.5368, -0.1843, -0.0, -1.5194, -0.0179, -1.5272, -0.005, -0.6248, -0.5439, -2.209, -0.02, -0