{"id": "491", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, or by going to Twitter.com and logging in with your Twitter username and password. Once logged in, click on your Twitter name, located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, then click on Settings and finally Blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. By setting this feature, you will receive an email notification whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nTo determine who liked your tweet, you need to identify the specific platform or service where the tweet was posted. Different platforms have different methods for displaying likes:\nThe reasoning steps are:\nIf the tweet was posted on a social media platform such as Twitter, you can find out who liked it by looking at the Like count under the tweet. However, if the tweet was posted on a platform that does not display likes in this way, such as LinkedIn, you may need to use a third-party tool or service to track likes.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 45.426, "generation_time_seconds": 30.0441, "selection_time_seconds": 15.3818, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [785, 3405, 17064, 1246, 311, 8253, 879, 14915, 264, 11809, 13, 2014, 4226, 419, 11, 582, 1184, 311, 2908, 279, 4419, 315, 279, 5339, 1380, 279, 11809, 572, 8454, 11, 438, 2155, 15409, 614, 2155, 5510, 315, 9027, 13151, 476, 21969, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.75, -0.4858, -0.0599, -0.3803, -0.0601, -0.021, -0.1183, -0.0028, -0.2554, -0.042, -0.0871, -0.6278, -0.3349, -0.0245, -0.0057, -0.1705, -0.0283, -0.0152, -0.7832, -