{"id": "619", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the information provided in the passages, here are the steps to force remove a printer in Devices and Printers:\n\n1. Open Print Manager or Printers folder.\n2. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete. If you can't delete the printer, run the command with administrative privileges by right-clicking the printer again and selecting \"Run as administrator\" before deleting it.\n3. Alternatively, you can remove the printer from the devices list, uninstall the Windows print drivers, and disconnect the printer from the computer if it's connected via USB. Restart the Spooler Service after removing the printer or printer port.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nSearch through the given passages for any information related to removing a printer from devices and printers.\nVerify if the passages contain any specific instructions or tools needed for the removal process.\nSince the question is about how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers, I should search for any mention of such a process in the given passages.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 49.302, "generation_time_seconds": 25.4691, "selection_time_seconds": 23.8325, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 943, 315, 22380, 1660, 14078, 13, 576, 7354, 369, 16652, 2578, 1745, 10078, 11649, 389, 3425, 432, 594, 264, 6961, 22380, 8433, 311, 264, 6366, 476, 264, 4108, 22380, 304, 3162, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.8687, -0.0019, -0.0419, -4.1034, -0.0084, -0.0717, -3.8508, -3.6391, -1.4831, 