{"id": "649", "question": "color of urin meaning", "gt": "The color of urine can indicate different health conditions. Red urine may indicate the presence of blood and could be a sign of an infection or cancer. Deep purple urine can be a characteristic of porphyria, a rare disorder. The normal color of urine is pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the passage for details about the significance of urine color, focusing on any specific examples, comparisons, or general descriptions provided.\nLook for any specific mentions of urine color, such as the typical color when healthy and what it means if it's different.\nLook for any specific mentions of urine color, such as the typical color when healthy and what it means if it's different.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 38.12, "generation_time_seconds": 24.5211, "selection_time_seconds": 13.5987, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 2661, 46769, 369, 894, 6286, 315, 279, 1894, 315, 39235, 323, 1181, 7290, 13, 9192, 369, 894, 3151, 3565, 911, 1128, 7987, 315, 39235, 2578, 13216, 476, 3076, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.7068, -0.0472, -0.0159, -1.2488, -0.2191, -0.1425, -0.0673, -0.7146, -0.0096, -0.5906, -0.0332, -0.0044, -0.0058, -0.0729, -0.0331, -1.3271, -0.0519, -1.5717, -0.0069, -1.2635, -0.4171, -2.3289, -1.9017, -1.4839, -0.8221, -0.5354, -0.0001, -0.2868, -0.1188, -1.4001, -0.3618, -0.0973, -0.0749], "cumulative_logprob": -19.9618, "norm_logp": -0.6049, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 33}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [785, 32711, 7354, 525, 1447], "logp_list": [-0.6532, -2.8766, -0.0346, -0.0584, -0.6205], "cumulative_logprob": -4.2433, "norm_logp