38, -0.0908, -0.08, -0.4782, -0.0937, -0.0081, -0.5533, -0.7528, -3.2212, -0.5201, -0.0002, -4.6042, -2.9426, -0.0019, -0.0169, -0.9498, -1.4995, -1.7586, -1.9122, -0.2402, -1.4037, -0.3001, -0.0008, -0.0, 0.0, -0.1323, -0.0001, -0.0938, -0.0], "cumulative_logprob": -34.0179, "norm_logp": -0.2362, "input_len": 479, "output_tokens": 144}, {"phase": "final", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.6854, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.002, -0.0001, -0.0355, -0.0003], "cumulative_logprob": -0.7239, "norm_logp": -0.0804, "input_len": 182, "output_tokens": 9}], "output_tokens": 484, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "669", "question": "what happens when you breath in and out", "gt": "Sure! Here's my answer based on the given passages:\n\nWhen you breathe in, the diaphragm contracts and pulls downwards, increasing the volume of the chest cavity. This lowers the pressure inside the chest, allowing air to enter the lungs. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also contract, expanding the ribcage and further increasing the space in the chest cavity. Air enters the lungs through the windpipe (trachea) and fills the expanded lung tissue.\n\nWhen you breathe out, the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity, reducing the space in the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax, allowing the chest cavity to decrease in size. As the space in the chest cavity decreases, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of the lungs and windpipe, and then out of the nose or mouth.\n\nTherefore, when you breathe in and out, air enters the lungs during inhalation and leaves the lungs during exhalation.", "pred": "When you breathe in, the diaphragm contracts and moves downward, increasing the volume of the thoracic cavity. This causes the lungs to expand, and air is drawn into the lungs due to the pressure difference. During exhalation, the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward, reducing the volume of the thoracic cavity, which causes the lungs to contract and expel air.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: When you breathe in, the diaphragm contracts and moves downward, increasing the volume of the thoracic cavity. This causes the lungs to expand, and air is drawn into the lungs due to the pressure difference. During exhalation, the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward, reducing the volume of the thoracic cavity, which causes the lungs to contract and expel air.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nAnalyze the physiological processes involved in breathing, including the role of the diaphragm, intercostal muscles, and the movement of air in and out of the lungs.\nIdentify the specific actions of the diaphragm and intercostal muscles during inhalation and exhalation.\nIdentify the direction of air movement during inhalation and exhalation, explaining how it relates to the expansion and contraction of the thoracic cavity and lungs.\n\nAnswer: When you breathe in, the diaphragm contracts and moves downward, increasing the volume of the thoracic cavity. This causes the lungs to expand, and air is drawn into the lungs due to the pressure difference. During exhalation, the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward, reducing the volume of the thoracic cavity, which causes the lungs to contract and expel air.", "time_sec": 59.679, "generation_time_seconds": 28.5734, "selection_time_seconds": 31.1059, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [5501, 3410, 279, 2661, 46769, 311, 10354, 448, 279, 6358, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-4.3249, -0.1996, -0.0083, -2.4482, -0.0277, -2.5743, -0.8506, -0.057, -0.0161, -0.2074, -0.0491, -0.0006], "cumulative_logprob": -10.7638, "norm_logp": -0.897, "input_len": 140, "output_tokens": 12}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 21085, 369, 894, 27787, 476, 40841, 315, 279, 1882, 315, 25938, 304, 323, 700, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.7357, -0.017, -0.0063, -1.5631, -0.1474, -1.71, -1.9434, -1.3762, -0.4032, -0.3264, -0.157, -0.8067, -0.0047, -0.0631, -0.3427, -0.0003, -0.0011, -0.2169, -0.7273], "cumulative_logprob": -11.5485, "norm_logp": -0.6078, "input_len": 140, "output_tokens": 19}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [785, 4024, 3405, 374, 10161, 911, 1128, 8573, 979, 498, 36297, 304, 323, 700, 13, 576, 32711, 7354, 3897, 773, 3041, 653, 537, 2924, 894, 1995, 911, 279, 11364, 30865, 2337, 76673, 367, 323, 505, 11866, 367, 13, 576, 1790, 19819, 3019, 304, 279, 32711, 1882, 1035, 387, 311, 7512, 1493, 11364, 3118, 389, 279, 2661, 1995