{"id": "39", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, you can run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic, then scrape it off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior. You can then apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Afterward, rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. You can mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water, dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water. Some plastic may be extremely difficult to remove, in which case you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun and then peel it off. If not all plastic comes off, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the type of plastic debris present in the dryer.\nExamine the dryer's interior, focusing on areas where plastic debris is likely to accumulate, such as the lint tray, vents, and corners.\nIdentify the tools or methods suitable for removing specific types of plastic debris, ensuring they are safe and effective for the dryer's material and function.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 47.459, "generation_time_seconds": 29.0362, "selection_time_seconds": 18.423, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 70894, 279, 6993, 315, 279, 3405, 624, 785, 3405, 17064, 1246, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 4363, 22023, 311, 12188, 33998, 429, 702, 40065, 4766, 382], "logp_list": [-2.9834, -0.0067, -0.0486, -0.0008, -3.062, -0.0218, -2.116, -0.0114, 