{"id": "58", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building nests on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch using a staple gun. This will prevent birds from reaching those spaces they often choose to build their nests, which can block your ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease. (Passage 1:4)\n2. Install bird netting over the top of your light fixture to block the birds' access to it. Choose a netting that is non-flammable and safe to use around light bulbs, and make sure it is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds. (Passage 2:1)\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch. The sight of a predator can scare the birds away from the area and keep them from inhabiting your porch. Move the plastic hawk periodically to keep the birds from becoming accustomed to its presence. (Passage 3:1)\n\nTherefore, based on the provided passages, you can keep birds from building nests on your porch by using bird netting, installing bird netting over your light fixture, or mounting a plastic hawk near your porch.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nTo determine methods to prevent birds from building nests on your porch, consider the following steps based on common strategies and deterrent techniques:\nIdentify the type of birds you want to deter from nesting. Different birds have different nest-building habits and preferences. Understanding their behavior can help tailor your approach effectively.\nIdentify the specific reasons why the birds are attracted to your porch, such as easy access, availability of nesting materials, or the presence of food sources. This will help in selecting effective deterrents.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 65.094, "generation_time_seconds": 34.8109, "selection_time_seconds": 30.283, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [785, 2661, 3405, 374, 911, 26160, 19654, 504, 4752, 264, 22791, 389, 264, 44647, 13, 2014, 3410, 264, 11682, 4226, 11, 358, 1184, 311, 1795, 279, 32711, 7354, 323, 23643, 279, 6961, 3565, 3019, 553, 3019, 382], "logp_list": [-1.5254, -1.966, -0.2599, -1.67, -0.9519, -0.4691, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0814, -1.7901, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0432, -0.0033, -0.0251, -0.7612, -1.9855, -0.3561, -2.0323, -0.3629, -0.0851, -2.2894, -0.1661, -0.0585, -4.6121, -0.3974, -0.4751, -0.0028, -2.2528, -0.0746, -0.011, -0.1485, -0.0135, -0.1206, -0.0039, -0.0, -1.2939], "cumulative_logprob": -26.2893, "norm_logp": -0.7105, "input_len": 144, "output_tokens": 37}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [40, 4157, 3410, 264, 19819, 32711, 3019, 1576, 498, 614, 537, 3897, 894, 46769, 476, 5107, 2266, 369, 752, 311, 23643, 323, 4226, 279, 3405, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.2218, -2.9364, -0.7033, -1.114, -0.5269, -0.025, -0.0004, -2.1854, -3.9448, -0.0703, -0.0037, -0.1568, -0.0454, -0.1626, -1.7162, -3.0312, -0.4132, -0.4007, -0.4026, -0.0, -0.0329, -2.7568, -1.5445, -0.1606, -0.001, -0.1858, -1.0309], "cumulative_logprob": -26.7732, "norm_logp": -0.9916, "input_len": 144, "output_tokens": 27}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 8253, 5413, 311, 5358, 19654, 504, 4752, 95121, 389, 697, 44647, 11, 2908, 279, 2701, 7354, 3118, 389, 4185, 14830, 323, 82620, 12538, 1447], "logp_list": [-2.4183, -0.7752, -7.029, -0.0567, -0.0576, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.112, -0.1828, -0.0003, -1.0265, 0.0, -0.0024, -0.412, -0.0912, -0.0493, -0.2774, -1.2872, -0.0001, -2.0231, -0.7127, -2.0951, -2.3763, -3.0986, -0.1064], "cumulative_logprob": -24.1903, "norm_logp": -0.9676, "input_len": 144, "output_tokens": 25}, {"phase": "rollout", "be