{"id": "82", "question": "symptoms and causes of ibs", "gt": "Symptoms of irritable bowel syndrome include diarrhea (often described as violent episodes of diarrhea), constipation, constipation alternating with diarrhea, belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement, and a lot of gas or bloating. Causes of irritable bowel syndrome are unknown but it is believed to be due to a number of factors including alteration in gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.", "pred": "Symptoms of IBS include abdominal pain, bloating, gas, diarrhea, and constipation. Causes of IBS include stress, diet, and changes in the gut microbiome.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: Symptoms of IBS include abdominal pain, bloating, gas, diarrhea, and constipation. Causes of IBS include stress, diet, and changes in the gut microbiome.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nAnalyze the symptoms and causes of IBS mentioned in the given passages.\nIdentify the specific symptoms of IBS as described in the passages, noting any key words or phrases used to describe these symptoms.\nIdentify the specific causes of IBS mentioned in the passages, noting any key words or phrases used to describe these causes.\n\nAnswer: Symptoms of IBS include abdominal pain, bloating, gas, diarrhea, and constipation. Causes of IBS include stress, diet, and changes in the gut microbiome.", "time_sec": 39.252, "generation_time_seconds": 28.4008, "selection_time_seconds": 10.8516, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 1376, 13495, 323, 11137, 9733, 304, 279, 21085, 5435, 311, 358, 7347, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.996, -0.0033, -2.9925, -0.0556, -0.9299, -0.057, -1.3476, -0.0021, -0.0001, -1.1993, -0.6665, -0.0, 