{"id": "103", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "The various systems in the human body work together to ensure its normal functioning. For instance, the urinary system works with all other systems to clean the blood by removing waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. This includes organs like the kidneys and lower intestines. Similarly, the respiratory system also collaborates with all other systems to provide oxygen to all body parts and remove carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. The respiratory system comprises the nose, larynx, trachea, and lungs.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n- Identify the body systems mentioned in the passage\n- Explain how each system functions individually\n- Describe the interactions and dependencies between the systems\n- Provide specific examples of how systems work together to maintain homeostasis or support other functions\n- Ensure the explanation is based on the information provided in the passages\nExtract key information from the passages about individual body systems and their functions.\nAnalyze how specific systems interact with each other to support overall bodily functions.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 55.98, "generation_time_seconds": 27.0616, "selection_time_seconds": 28.918, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [12, 64547, 279, 2487, 5942, 9733, 304, 279, 21085, 198, 12, 81917, 1246, 1817, 1849, 5746, 31299, 198, 12, 60785, 279, 21880, 323, 19543, 1948, 279, 5942, 198, 12, 39565, 3151, 10295, 315, 1246, 5942, 975, 3786, 311, 10306, 2114, 535, 10718, 476, 1824, 1008, 5746, 198, 12, 29279, 27