{"id": "132", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, but keep the skins of the individual cloves intact. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves to expose them. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves. Season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices if you like. Roasting time is dependent on the size of the cloves and may take up to 45 minutes or an hour for larger cloves. Once roasted, the garlic cloves can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the preparation methods described in the passages for roasting garlic cloves.\nLook for specific instructions or methods mentioned for roasting individual garlic cloves in the passages.\nIdentify the method of roasting that is most suitable for individual garlic cloves.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 48.081, "generation_time_seconds": 26.7161, "selection_time_seconds": 21.3648, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [19432, 279, 3897, 46769, 369, 894, 11221, 476, 5413, 389, 926, 14725, 3842, 30635, 84288, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-4.6404, -0.0035, -1.1625, -0.0481, -0.3025, -0.1279, -1.2904, -0.0532, -0.337, -1.5509, -0.04, 0.0, -0.0937, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0072, -0.4796], "cumulative_logprob": -10.1369, "norm_logp": -0.5963, "input_len": 138, "output_tokens": 17}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3151, 7354, 476, 5413, 9733, 304, 27