{"id": "141", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\nAccording to passage 1, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This reduction is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act.\n\nPassage 3 further states that the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset (i.e., opening WDV of such asset less scrap value) even though such discarded asset is not used for the purposes of business or profession in such year and subsequent years.\n\nTherefore, the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is to reduce the block value of the asset by the scrap value in the previous year in which it is discarded, and to claim depreciation on the residual value of the asset in the year of discard and subsequent years.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nBased on the given passage, the treatment for an asset discarded under the Income Tax Act would be the following:\nThis step involves identifying the relevant information from the given passage that pertains to the treatment of an asset discarded under the Income Tax Act. The task is to extract specific details about how assets are treated when discarded, likely including any relevant tax implications, such as capital gains or losses, or the timing of recognition for tax purposes.\nThe question asks about the treatment when an asset is discarded under the Income Tax Act. To answer this, we need to identify the specific provisions or rules in the Income Tax Act that govern the treatment of discarded assets. This includes understanding how the asset's value, if any, is treated for tax purposes, whether it is subject to capital gains tax, and how the disposal is reported for tax returns. The answer should also consider whether there are any exceptions or special rules for certain types of assets (e.g., business assets vs. personal assets) and any accounting methods that might be relevant.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 50.394, "generation_time_seconds": 39.4764, "selection_time_seconds": 10.9172, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 70894, 279, 2266, 323, 279, 3151, 3239, 624, 785, 1196, 374, 10161, 911, 279, 6380, 315, 458, 9329, 979, 432, 374, 43210, 11, 438, 817, 279, 7911, 3742, 1160, 13, 1096, 23945, 582, 1184, 311, 1477, 1995, 5435, 311, 9329, 33445, 304, 279, 2266, 315, 3742, 6872, 382], "logp_list": [-2.2138, -0.0028, -0.0569, -0.0012, -3.318, -0.0101, -0.2383, -1.8893, -0.3465, -0.4185, -2.15, -1.6466, -0.0802, -4.002, -0.0392, -0.0305, -0.0139, -0.002, -0.1158, -0.0771, -0.1143, -0.0, -0.2259, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0001, -1.7662, -0.8035, -0.0277, -0.0009, -3.1055, -0.0, -0.0063, -0.2727, -0.1356, -0.9825, -1.0907, -0.0257, -0.006, -1.2322, -0.1738, -0.7303, -0.0, -1.7045, -0.0033, -1.8968, -0.0575, -0.522, -0.0, -1.4591, -0.9394, -0.0303], "cumulative_logprob": -33.9667, "norm_logp": -0.6532, "input_len": 145, "output_tokens": 52}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3151, 19156, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 8826, 279, 33445, 315, 11770, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.4996, -0.0047, -0.0782, -0.4464, -2.2426, -0.7211, -0.0002, -0.0957, -0.0, -0.0, -3.0415, -0.0437, -1.1192, -0.0342, -0.0011, -0.4348, -0.0862], "cumulative_logprob": -9.8492, "norm_logp": -0.5794, "input_len": 145, "output_tokens": 17}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [5501, 3410, 279, 21085, 369, 6358, 13, 151645], "