{"id": "194", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to attach multiple picture frames together:\n\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding (Passage 1).\n2. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect (Passage 1).\n3. Mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides of the frames, making sure the placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame (Passage 1).\n4. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames (Passage 1).\n5. Test ideas by laying the group of multiple pictures out on the floor first (Passage 2).\n6. Screw the frame to the backer board, repeat with each frame, and attach a hanging wire to the back (Passage 3).\n\nIt's important to note that the passages do not provide specific information on how to attach multiple frames together other than the steps mentioned above. Therefore, if more detailed instructions are needed, it may be best to consult additional resources or seek advice from a professional framer.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nLook for specific methods or tools mentioned in the passages for attaching multiple picture frames together.\nLook for any examples or instructions provided in the passages on how to assemble the frames, such as the use of hinges or adhesive material.\nIdentify any warnings or precautions related to the attachment process, such as ensuring the frames are spaced correctly or choosing the appropriate type of adhesive or hardware.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 72.061, "generation_time_seconds": 31.4837, "selection_time_seconds": 40.5767, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [37175, 279, 315