{"id": "216", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to properly wash wine glasses:\n\n1. If hot water and mild detergent cannot remove wine residue, use baking soda to dissolve and loosen the adhesive residue (Passage 1).\n2. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles and rinse thoroughly with hot water (Passage 2).\n3. For hand cleaning, lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water and wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage (Passage 3). Use a small amount of detergent and only in the bottom of the glass and around the rim to avoid flavoring future wine. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, first examine them for any visible dirt, stains, or residue. Use a gentle, non-abrasive sponge or cloth to clean the exterior and interior surfaces of the wine glasses. Rinse the wine glasses under running water to remove any remaining dirt or residue from the cleaning process.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first examine them for any visible dirt, stains, or residue. Use a gentle, non-abrasive sponge or cloth to clean the exterior and interior surfaces of the wine glasses. Rinse the wine glasses under running water to remove any remaining dirt or residue from the cleaning process.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the wine glasses for any visible dirt, stains, or residue.\nUse a gentle, non-abrasive sponge or cloth to clean the exterior and interior surfaces of the wine glasses.\nRinse the wine glasses under running water to remove any remaining dirt or residue from the cleaning process.\n\nAnswer: To wash wine glasses properly, first examine them for any visible dirt, stains, or residue. Use a gentle, non