{"id": "318", "question": "how can i check taxes were filed", "gt": "Based on the given passages, you can check the status of your tax return by:\n\n1. Using the IRS2Go app on your smartphone to check the status of your tax return online.\n2. Checking the status of your tax return over the phone by calling the IRS.\n3. Checking the status of your state tax return online or over the phone.\n\nTo check the status of your tax return, you will need your Social Security number, tax filing status, and the amount of any refund due. If you e-filed your return, you can check the status 24 hours after the IRS acknowledged receipt of your return. If you mailed your taxes, you will have to wait 3 or 4 weeks after mailing in your taxes.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to check taxes were filed is:\n\nYou can check the status of your tax return online or over the phone using the methods described above.", "pred": "To check if taxes were filed, you can visit the website of the tax authority in your country.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: To check if taxes were filed, you can visit the website of the tax authority in your country.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nPassage: It is important to ensure that your taxes have been filed correctly to avoid penalties. You can check the status of your tax filing by visiting the website of the tax authority in your country.\nThe passage provides a specific method to check the status of tax filing: by visiting the website of the tax authority in your country.\nThe next logical reasoning step is to identify the specific action required to visit the tax authority's website.\n\nAnswer: To check if taxes were filed, you can visit the website of the tax authority in your country.", "time_sec": 53.618, "generation_time_seconds": 26.948, "selection_time_seconds": 26.6704, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam":