{"id": "405", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nTo remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, you should follow these steps:\n\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw located in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\n\nIt is important to note that an instructional video is also available that shows the entire process and location of the screws and pin.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nWhat specific part of the door panel is being discussed in the question?\nThe specific part of the door panel being discussed in the question is the door panel removal process for a 2006 Chevrolet vehicle.\nWhat type of information is required to answer the question about removing the 2006 Chevrolet's door panel?\nThe required information includes detailed steps or instructions on how to remove the door panel, possibly with specific tools or parts mentioned.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 57.597, "generation_time_seconds": 29.0535, "selection_time_seconds": 28.5431, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3151, 5479, 315, 279, 220, 17, 15, 15, 21, 57298, 429, 1184, 311, 387, 6963, 979, 4633, 700, 279, 6006, 6945, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.561, -0.0019, -0.0343, -0.1318, -3.1766, -0.1726, -0.0081, -0.1457, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.6085, -0.4589, -0.454, -0.03, -0.0001, -0.0561, -2.3708, -0.0412, -0.8131, -0.0169, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0241, -0.0144], "cumulative_logprob": -10.1206, "norm_logp": -