{"id": "438", "question": "how to find someone in france", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to find someone in France:\n\n1. Check the French White Pages (in English): You can use the website pagesjaunes.fr to search for people in France. To search for someone in Paris or its suburbs, enter \"IDF\" (Ile de France) in the department or region field instead of typing Paris.\n2. Use the nom field to enter the last name of the person you are looking for, and you can also include their first name in the prenom field.\n3. Provide address information, if known, in the ou section to refine your search.\n4. Click \"trouver\" to search for the name, and the search results will display name, address, and phone number for all listings that match your search criteria.\n\nNote that the effectiveness of these methods may depend on how up-to-date the information in the white pages is and whether the person you are looking for has listed their contact information publicly.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nGiven the question \"how to find someone in france\", the logical reasoning steps to follow would be:\nIdentify the relevant information in the given passages that may pertain to finding someone in France.\nAnalyze each relevant passage for specific methods or tools used to find someone in France.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 38.71, "generation_time_seconds": 28.165, "selection_time_seconds": 10.5445, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 7428, 315, 279, 2711, 25, 2160, 432, 311, 1477, 4325, 369, 264, 4345, 3947, 11, 311, 3645, 1105, 369, 2562, 7966, 11, 476, 369, 1008, 3151, 3880, 30, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.51, -0.0056, -0.1713, -4.1496, -0.3836, 