{"id": "492", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, there are several ways to track who likes your tweets:\n\n1. Favotter.net and Favstar.fm - These websites allow you to track who has favorited your tweets and which tweets have been favorited by multiple users. (Passage 1)\n2. Using a web-based website - There are websites that allow you to check Twitter users who favorite tweets. (Passage 2)\n3. On Twitter - You can set up your account settings to receive notifications via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is: You can use Favotter.net, Favstar.fm, or a web-based website to track who likes your tweets, or you can set up your Twitter account settings to receive email notifications.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nStep 1: Understand the question\nThe question asks how one can determine who liked their tweet.\nStep 2: Identify the context and the given information\nThe context is about social media interactions, specifically liking a tweet. There is no specific information provided in the passages about how to determine who liked a tweet.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 40.586, "generation_time_seconds": 28.4431, "selection_time_seconds": 12.1432, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [12549, 279, 3405, 374, 911, 25597, 879, 14915, 264, 11809, 11, 323, 279, 4226, 1969, 387, 14257, 504, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1077, 594, 23643, 279, 32711, 7354, 1447], "logp_list": [-6.0357, -0.0529, -0.0918, -1.0166, -0.2647, -2.1317, -0.0345, -0.0008, -0.2978, -0.0203, -0.0218, -1.6097, -0.178, -5.1781, -2.9172, -0.0912, -2.