{"id": "507", "question": "what are the characteristics of tropical rainforest floor", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor are:\n\n1. High levels of rainfall, with some areas receiving up to 400 inches of rain annually.\n2. High humidity due to the large amount of rainfall.\n3. Abundant vegetation, including tall trees, vines, ferns, herbs, mushrooms, fruits, and nuts.\n4. Quick decay of plant and animal matter due to the heat and moisture, which provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow.\n5. Presence of bananas growing on vines.\n\nTherefore, the tropical rainforest floor is characterized by high rainfall, humidity, and lush vegetation, with a diverse array of plant species and a rapid rate of decay and nutrient cycling.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify and list the physical characteristics of a tropical rainforest floor based on the passage.\nLook for specific details about the vegetation, soil, and other physical features of the tropical rainforest floor mentioned in the passage.\nLook for any mention of the growth patterns or types of plants found on the floor of the tropical rainforest as described in the passage.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 50.381, "generation_time_seconds": 26.8601, "selection_time_seconds": 23.5206, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 323, 1140, 279, 6961, 17452, 315, 264, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 3118, 389, 279, 21085, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.6044, -0.0039, -3.4717, -0.9725, -0.1871, -2.6355, -0.594, -0.2618, -3.453, -0.0524, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0016, -1.6032, -0.0001, -0.0512, -3.7461, -0.1357, -0.0249], "cumulative_logprob": -18.7992, "norm_logp": -0.9894, "inp