{"id": "50", "question": "benefits of a water pick", "gt": "A water pick, also known as a Waterpik, is a beneficial tool for oral care. It is designed to shoot a strong stream of water at the gum line to help eliminate germs and plaque that are tough to get rid of with a toothbrush. It can also help maintain overall body health. In comparison to flossing, using a water pick can be easier and leave your mouth feeling cleaner. It can also massage and stimulate soft tissue in the mouth, reducing the risk of gingivitis. It is especially useful in cleaning around the teeth and gums, removing food from areas that brushing cannot reach.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the specific benefits of a water pick as mentioned in the passages. Look for details such as improved oral hygiene, ease of use, and any specific conditions it can help manage.\nIdentify specific examples or comparisons mentioned in the passages regarding the benefits of a water pick.\nAnalyze the information about the use and effectiveness of a water pick in comparison to traditional brushing methods. Identify any scientific studies or expert opinions mentioned regarding the benefits of water picks.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 49.843, "generation_time_seconds": 31.7078, "selection_time_seconds": 18.1348, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 23643, 279, 6961, 3565, 3019, 553, 3019, 369, 279, 7567, 315, 264, 3015, 3735, 11, 582, 1184, 311, 2908, 279, 2701, 13566, 1447], "logp_list": [-3.9606, -1.9143, -0.0038, -1.2653, -0.0003, -0.1389, -0.0056, -0.0, -2.0489, -0.0231, -0.8271, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.046, -0.6172, -0.329, -0.003, -0.5178, -0.1831, -0.0806, -0.6483, -0.0841], "cumulative_logprob"