{"id": "94", "question": "what is the difference between essential and nonessential amino acids", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main differences between essential and non-essential amino acids are:\n\nEssential Amino Acids:\n\n* Must be obtained from the diet\n* Cannot be produced by the body\n* Nine out of 20 amino acids are considered essential (valine, isoleucine, leucine, lysine, methionine, phenylalanine, threonine, tryptophan, and histidine for infants)\n\nNon-Essential Amino Acids:\n\n* Can be produced by the body\n* Not necessarily required to obtain from the diet\n* Include alanine, asparagine, aspartic acid, glutamic acid, arginine, cysteine, glutamine, glycine, ornithine, proline, serine, and tyrosine\n\nIt is important to note that even though non-essential amino acids can be produced by the body, it is still important to consume a balanced diet that includes all of the essential amino acids to ensure proper bodily functions.", "pred": "Essential amino acids are those that the body cannot produce on its own and must be obtained through the diet. Nonessential amino acids, on the other hand, can be synthesized by the body from other amino acids. Essential amino acids are crucial for growth and repair of tissues, while nonessential amino acids play a role in various bodily functions, including protein synthesis and energy production.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Essential amino acids are those that the body cannot produce on its own and must be obtained through the diet. Nonessential amino acids, on the other hand, can be synthesized by the body from other amino acids. Essential amino acids are crucial for growth and repair of tissues, while nonessential amino acids play a role in various bodily functions, including protein synthesis and energy production.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the definitions and roles of essential and nonessential amino acids as explained in the passage.\nIdentify the specific characteristics or functions of essential amino acids that distinguish them from nonessential amino acids.\nCompare the functions and requirements of essential amino acids in the body to those of nonessential amino acids.\n\nEssential amino acids are those that the body cannot produce on its own and must be obtained through the diet. Nonessential amino acids, on the other hand, can be synthesized by the body from other amino acids. Essential amino acids are crucial for growth and repair of tissues, while nonessential amino acids play a role in various bodily functions, including protein synthesis and energy production.", "time_sec": 47.46, "generation_time_seconds": 28.809, "selection_time_seconds": 18.6512, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3405, 11, 279, 32711, 7354, 1265, 1156, 21101, 279, 7271, 315, 1817, 943, 315, 41400, 13621, 382], "logp_list": [-3.9395, -0.0001, -0.002, -1.0556, -0.1678, -0.4489, -1.5662, -0.1899, -0.8692, -4.7861, -6.5764, -0.2675, -1.9775, -0.2309, -4.1506, -0.0494, -0.0009, -0.0004, -0.0039, -4.1173], "cumulative_logprob": -30.4001, "norm_logp": -1.52, "input_len": 143, "output_tokens": 20}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 7271, 315, 7565, 41400, 32869, 323, 2477, 48482, 41400, 32869, 438, 4512, 304, 279, 21085, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.5288, -0.079, -0.0062, -1.2402, -0.8381, -0.0251, -0.252, -0.0, -0.3955, -0.1099, -0.0115, -0.0, -0.0, -2.0197, -7.4561, -0.0306, -0.0011, -0.7011, -0.0329, -0.3582], "cumulative_logprob": -15.086, "norm_logp": -0.7543, "input_len": 143, "output_tokens": 20}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 17473, 323, 12783, 315, 7565, 323, 2477, 48482, 41400, 32869, 438, 11247, 304, 279, 21085, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.5288, -0.079, -0.0062, -1.3295, -0.8505, -0.9503, -0.0103, -0.026, -0.0163, 0.0, -0.0023, -0.0, -0.0, -1