{"id": "104", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "The body systems work together in order to maintain the normal functioning of the human body. These systems include the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems. Each system has its own specific functions, but they also work in conjunction with one another to ensure the overall well-being of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from various systems such as the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. Similarly, the respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nAnalyze the specific parts of the given passages that discuss the interaction between body systems.\nIdentify the key systems mentioned and their interactions described in the passages.\nSummarize the interactions between systems mentioned in the passages, focusing on how they support each other functionally.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 55.988, "generation_time_seconds": 25.9365, "selection_time_seconds": 30.0519, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [852, 678, 279, 2487, 5942, 9733, 304, 279, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-5.0519, -2.6885, -0.1468, -0.1635, -0.0002, -0.2629, -0.0068, -0.0, -1.3698, -0.1868, -0.0739, -0.0018], "cumulative_logprob": -9.9529, "norm_logp": -0.8294, "input_len": 138, "output_tokens": 12}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3151, 5942, 9733, 304, 279, 3405, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.