{"id": "133", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "To roast individual garlic cloves, preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the garlic bulb, leaving the skins of the cloves intact. Cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of the cloves to expose them. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up, and drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, rubbing it over the cloves. Roast the cloves in the preheated oven for about 45 minutes to an hour, or until they are softened. Store the roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the given passages for any explicit instructions or techniques for roasting individual garlic cloves.\nLook for any sections discussing preparation methods or cooking techniques that could be applied to roasting garlic cloves individually.\nLook for any specific advice on handling garlic cloves before roasting, such as peeling or trimming.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 46.535, "generation_time_seconds": 25.1937, "selection_time_seconds": 21.3417, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 3897, 46769, 369, 3151, 11221, 476, 5413, 369, 926, 14725, 3842, 30635, 84288, 13, 9192, 369, 3565, 1741, 438, 9315, 11, 882, 11, 476, 17975, 5413, 429, 525, 9733, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.069, -0.0471, -0.0169, -1.3664, -0.0581, -0.097, -2.3614, -0.0381, -0.2727, -0.2137, -0.7294, -0.0002, 0.0, -0.0936, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0098, -0.7456, -0.0002, -0.4186, -0.3341, 0.0, -0.4735, -0.3465, -0.874, -0.0092, -0.5485, -2.1185, -0.8543, -2.0505, -0.2054, -0.1596, -0.13, -0.1748], "cumulative_logprob": -15.8