{"id": "142", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\nThe scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded, as per Section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. The block concept applies to all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation, and any alterations to the value of the block must be made in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act. The assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset (i.e., opening WDV of such asset less scrap value) even if the asset is not used for business or professional purposes in that year or subsequent years.\n\nTherefore, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is to reduce the scrap value from the block in the previous year and claim depreciation on the residual value.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the specific sections of the Income Tax Act that address the treatment of assets when they are discarded. Identify any relevant provisions regarding the recording of the disposal of assets and the implications for tax purposes.\nExamine the specific sections of the Income Tax Act that address the treatment of assets when they are discarded. Identify any relevant provisions regarding the recording of the disposal of assets and the implications for tax purposes. Look for details on how the disposal affects the company's taxable income and any necessary reporting requirements.\nExamine specific cases or examples provided in the Income Tax Act that illustrate the treatment of assets when discarded. Identify how the disposal is recorded, the impact on taxable income, and any reporting requirements outlined for such events.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 44.652, "generation_time_seconds": 34.022, "selection_time_seconds": 10.6299, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [12, 64547, 279, 3151, 19156, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 5435, 311, 9329, 33445, 323, 6380, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-5.5174, -0.7021, -0.0909, -0.4552, -2.5251, -0.4844, -0.0002, -0.0691, -0.0, -0.0, -0.4812, 0.0, -2.4303, -0.0144, -1.825, -0.4218, -1.726, -0.0183], "cumulative_logprob": -16.7614, "norm_logp": -0.9312, "input_len": 145, "output_tokens": 18}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [2082, 55856, 279, 3151, 19156, 315, 279, 7911, 3742, 1160, 8826, 279, 6380, 315, 11770, 429, 525, 43210, 13, 9192, 369, 894, 6286, 315, 93089, 11, 33445, 11, 476, 3270, 12462, 15966, 429, 3796, 311, 1741, 11770, 13, 1416, 279, 1160, 5707, 3151, 11221, 11, 807, 1265, 387, 21870, 5961, 13, 1416, 432, 1558, 537, 11, 8253, 421, 1052, 525, 894, 9760, 23168, 10659, 476, 14305, 429, 2578, 3796, 311, 279, 6380, 315, 43210, 11770, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-4.1781, -0.0, -0.0219, -0.1285, -1.0802, -0.277, -0.0011, -2.9215, -0.0, -0.0045, -1.0367, -0.17, -0.4676, -0.0004, -0.0446, -1.7441, -0.0233, -0.0008, -0.1011, -0.8731, -0.0003, -0.3086, -0.8046, -0.0003, -0.5748, -0.0635, -2.9853, -0.2321, -0.0333, -1.158, -0.1171, -0.2138, -3.3647, -0.1245, -0.0539, -0.3712, -0.0485, -0.0034, -4.192, -0.2377, -0.2921, -1.7181, -1.5104, -0.8648, -0.761, -3.9743, -0.0273, -0.0025, -2.0035, -1.2354, -0.1578, -0.0969, -4.361, -0.2089, -0.0, -0.8243, -2.1584, -0.345, -0.2343, -0.1123, -0.1275, -2.0844, -1.5386, -0.2222, -0.0792, -0.7456, -0.0016, -2.0166, -0.6656, -2.4358, -0.2099, -0.6162, -0.0009, -0.152, -0.0, -0.8357, -0.1516], "cumulative_logprob": -60.7338, "norm_logp": -0.7888, "input_len": 145, "output_tokens": 77}, {