{"id": "167", "question": "show me how can i make gragh for my research", "gt": "To create a graph for your research, you first need to collect all of your data, remembering that the graph should show a comparison among categories. If you are creating a bar graph, you will use rectangular bars to represent different values. You need to title your graph and determine how high your graph needs to go. If your data points are substantially different in scale, you can use a pie chart. The y-axis of your graph will have a scale, and each bar’s height should be proportionate to the size of the category it represents. Make sure to consider any disproportionate responses that might impact the scale of your graph. Regardless of the type of graph you choose, it should provide a clear visual representation of your information.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the types of graphs commonly used in research and identify the most appropriate one for your specific data.\nIdentify the specific type of data you are working with (categorical, numerical, time series, etc.) and how it will influence the graph type.\nChoose a graphing tool or software that suits your needs and familiarity, such as Microsoft Excel, Google Sheets, or specialized software like MATLAB or R.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 54.603, "generation_time_seconds": 32.5639, "selection_time_seconds": 22.0394, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 943, 315, 4771, 4362, 369, 279, 3412, 821, 25, 22201, 279, 8311, 4771, 943, 3118, 389, 279, 6993, 315, 279, 821, 323, 279, 3412, 3405, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 990, 264, 1555, 4771, 369, 19259, 821, 11, 264, 3619, 4771, 369, 69536, 821, 11, 323, 264, 4349, 9487, 369, 902