{"id": "276", "question": "what is severe osteoporosis", "gt": "Severe osteoporosis is a condition characterized by significant bone density loss, resulting in weakened bones and increased risk of fractures. Symptoms may include sudden and severe back pain, loss of height over time, fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones. Without treatment, fractures, particularly in the spine or hips, are likely to occur.", "pred": "Severe osteoporosis is a condition characterized by a significant loss of bone density, leading to an increased risk of fractures. It is often associated with a low bone mineral density (BMD) that is more than 2.5 standard deviations below the young adult mean. This condition can result in bone fragility and increased susceptibility to fractures, even from minor impacts or without any apparent cause.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Severe osteoporosis is a condition characterized by a significant loss of bone density, leading to an increased risk of fractures. It is often associated with a low bone mineral density (BMD) that is more than 2.5 standard deviations below the young adult mean. This condition can result in bone fragility and increased susceptibility to fractures, even from minor impacts or without any apparent cause.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the definition of osteoporosis provided in the passage.\nIdentify the criteria or symptoms that are associated with severe osteoporosis mentioned in the passage.\nIdentify the specific characteristics or indicators of severe osteoporosis mentioned in the passage.\n\nSevere osteoporosis is a condition characterized by a significant loss of bone density, leading to an increased risk of fractures. It is often associated with a low bone mineral density (BMD) that is more than 2.5 standard deviations below the young adult mean. This condition can result in bone fragility and increased susceptibility to fractures, even from minor impacts or without any apparent cause.", "time_sec": 48.966, "generation_time_seconds": 29.2214, "selection_time_seconds": 19.7447, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [2082, 55856, 279, 7271, 315, 15386, 51268, 88666, 10704, 3897, 304, 279, 21085, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-4.2926, -0.0, -0.0082, -0.4197, -0.5596, -0.1361, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -1.5628, -0.0046, -0.0014, -0.269, -0.2095, -0.1385], "cumulative_logprob": -7.602, "norm_logp": -0.5068, "input_len": 138, "output_tokens": 15}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [10380, 369, 264, 7271, 476, 4008, 315, 15386, 51268, 88666, 10704, 304, 279, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.1319, -0.0394, -0.25, -0.0917, -0.1567, -0.3396, -0.0067, -0.0192, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0489, -0.0007, -2.34, -0.4744, -0.015], "cumulative_logprob": -6.9142, "norm_logp": -0.4321, "input_len": 138, "output_tokens": 16}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 7271, 315, 51268, 88666, 10704, 3897, 304, 279, 21085, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.9712, -0.047, -0.0082, -0.473, -0.5622, -1.5084, -0.0, -0.0, -0.826, -0.0019, -0.0006, -0.2788, -0.4439, -0.2052], "cumulative_logprob": -6.3264, "norm_logp": -0.4519, "input_len": 138, "output_tokens": 14}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [785, 32711, 7354, 525, 1447], "logp_list": [-2.7748, -0.9701, -0.0355, -0.0641, -0.9034], "cumulative_logprob": -4.7479, "norm_logp": -0.9496, "input_len": 138, "output_tokens": 5}, {"phase": "vote", "beam": null, "token_ids": [24728, 220, 16, 25, 37427, 2986, 279, 7271, 315, 15386, 51268, 88666, 10704, 3897, 304, 279, 21085, 382, 24728, 220, 17, 25, 9192, 369, 264, 7271, 476, 4008, 315, 15386, 51268, 88666, 10704, 304, 279, 46769, 382, 24728, 220, 18, 25, 1374, 19991, 279, 7271, 315, 51268, 88666, 10704, 3897, 304, 279, 21085, 382, 24728, 220, 19, 25, 576, 32711, 7354, 525, 1447, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 1447, 16141, 25, 27107, 220