{"id": "290", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven:\n\n1. Defrost the pork loin if possible. If you don't have time to defrost, you can place it in the oven at 250°F for about an hour.\n2. Preheat the oven to 325°F (passage 2).\n3. Rub the surface of the frozen pork loin with 2 tsp of olive oil and season the outside with salt, pepper, and desired herbs (thyme, oregano, or garlic work well) (passage 2).\n4. Place the pork loin in a roasting pan and put it in the preheated oven (passage 2).\n5. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound, or until the internal temperature reaches 150°F (passage 3).\n6. Use a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature of the meat (passage 3).\n7. Once the meat is cooked, remove it from the oven and cover it with aluminum foil for 30 minutes before serving (passage 3).\n\nNote that the exact cooking time may vary depending on the size of the roast, so adjust the cooking time accordingly. Also, make sure to check the internal temperature of the meat to ensure that it is cooked all the way through.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nLook for cooking instructions in the passage that mention how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven.\nLook for specific cooking methods, such as preheating the oven or using a specific temperature and time range, that are relevant to cooking a frozen pork loin roast in the oven.\nLook for step-by-step directions in the passage that outline the process for cooking a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, including specific oven temperatures and cooking times.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 52.625, "generation_time_seconds": 26.535