{"id": "335", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\n\n1. Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, which are common hiding places for ticks. (Passage 1)\n2. Use tick control products recommended by a veterinarian to prevent ticks from attaching to the dog. (Passage 2)\n3. Remove ticks from the dog using a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages whether there are any specific products or methods for getting rid of ticks from dogs that are already infested.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the given passages for any direct or indirect information about methods for removing ticks from dogs. Look for specific techniques, products, or advice provided in the text.\nCheck if the passages mention any preventative measures such as using tick collars, monthly treatments, or other methods to prevent ticks from attaching to dogs in the first place.\nIdentify any references to common tick removal techniques such as using tweezers, rubbing alcohol, or specialized tick removal devices mentioned in the text.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 47.886, "generation_time_seconds": 31.6828, "selection_time_seconds": 16.2027, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [3862, 525, 3807, 5413, 311, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 2670, 1667, 65276, 9341, 3871, 11, 1667, 20655, 29910, 11, 323, 1667, 12158, 2524, 10953, 13, 6909, 938, 9341, 3871, 11, 1741, 438, 95855, 323, 9341, 8151, 942, 323, 557, 53730, 436, 11, 646, 387, 9251, 5961, 311, 279, 5562, 594, 6787, 323, 22875, 311, 5505, 29957, 13