{"id": "395", "question": "why should we serve others", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"Why should we serve others?\"\n\nWe should serve others because it is a way to show love and kindness to everyone, even those who may not treat us well. Serving others is an expression of our love for God and our desire to be like Him. When we truly know God, our natural response is a desire to love and serve Him in return, and serving others is a way to do so. Additionally, serving others without self-serving motives and expecting nothing in return allows us to serve out of love and build stronger character muscles.\n\nTherefore, serving others is not only a way to show love and kindness, but it is also a way to deepen our relationship with God and grow in our faith.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the key reasons or values that support the idea of serving others.\nAnalyze the potential benefits of serving others, including personal growth, community improvement, and societal harmony.\nResearch and list the specific examples or studies that highlight the positive impact of serving others on individuals and communities.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 31.83, "generation_time_seconds": 22.726, "selection_time_seconds": 9.1042, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-4.0021, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0051, -0.0001], "cumulative_logprob": -4.0083, "norm_logp": -0.4454, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 9}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3151, 1995, 304, 279, 46769, 5435, 311, 13480, 3800, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.3235, -0