{"id": "406", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nTo remove the door panel on a 2006 Chevy, you will need to:\n\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin that holds the panel in place on the outer edge of the door.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\n5. Remove any wiring connections.\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n\nAfter removing the screws and clips, you will be able to remove the door panel. It is recommended to watch an instructional video to see the process and locate the parts mentioned.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nStep 1: Analyze the question for the specific details it requires.\nThe question asks about removing a door panel from a 2006 Chevrolet vehicle. It does not specify which model of 2006 Chevrolet.\nStep 2: Examine the given passages for information related to removing a door panel from a 2006 Chevrolet.\nSince the question does not specify a particular model, we need to identify if the passage mentions any Chevrolet vehicles from the year 2006 and their door panel removal process. Look for any mentions of Chevrolet models or specific instructions related to door panel removal.\nStep 3: Look for explicit instructions or methods for removing a door panel in the 2006 Chevrolet vehicle from the given passages.\nIdentify any specific steps or tools mentioned for removing a door panel in a 2006 Chevrolet vehicle. Note any diagrams, numbers, or comparisons that are relevant to the process.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 49.4, "generation_time_seconds": 36.0648, "selection_time_se