{"id": "508", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "gt": "Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and contain more of the tenderloin or fillet than sirloin steaks. They are essentially a larger version of the T-Bone steak, carved from a larger portion of the tenderloin. On the other hand, the sirloin steak is a steak cut from the back of the animal, continuing off the short loin from which T-bone, porterhouse, and club steaks are cut. The sirloin is divided into several different types of steak.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the key physical differences between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak.\nLocate the physical details about sirloin steak and porterhouse steak in the passage.\nAnalyze the specific physical characteristics mentioned for each steak type in the passage.\n\nThe passage does not provide specific physical differences between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak. Therefore, I cannot answer the question based on the given information.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 37.266, "generation_time_seconds": 23.1411, "selection_time_seconds": 14.1245, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 1376, 6961, 11799, 1948, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 323, 87186, 7675, 48959, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.4314, -0.0019, -0.033, -1.5752, -0.3424, -1.9893, -0.0349, -0.3783, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0665, -0.0, -0.0003, 0.0, -0.0, -1.0731, -0.0458], "cumulative_logprob": -6.9721, "norm_logp": -0.4101, "input_len": 145, "output_tokens": 17}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [785, 1790, 19819, 32711, 3019, 374, 311, 9429, 279, 1378, 4087, 9810, 553, 37836, 862, 6961, 17452, 11, 15104,