{"id": "609", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "To create employee schedules, start by making a list of all employees and the tasks they can perform. Then, create a chart with the work days and hours for each day. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper to do this. Afterward, print out copies for employees or send schedules to their email accounts. It's also important to maintain a master schedule for making any necessary changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, which can be modified as your business expands.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the key components of employee schedules.\nExamine the given passages for any specific methods or guidelines on creating employee schedules.\nLook for examples or detailed explanations in the passages about the creation or adjustment of employee schedules.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 45.64, "generation_time_seconds": 25.7614, "selection_time_seconds": 19.8789, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [2082, 55856, 279, 3405, 323, 10542, 279, 1376, 5424, 25, 330, 12946, 36769, 1189, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.2544, -0.0, -0.0081, -1.0242, -2.4037, -0.4814, -0.1387, -0.3197, -1.0108, -0.1878, -0.421, -0.9628, -0.0028, -1.1017, -0.6397], "cumulative_logprob": -11.9568, "norm_logp": -0.7971, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 15}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 1376, 6813, 315, 279, 3405, 13, 576, 3405, 17064, 911, 1246, 311, 1855, 9364, 36769, 11, 21080, 389, 279, 1882, 476, 5413, 6398, 304, 3730, 773, 624, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 37427, 2986, 279, 2661, 46769, 311, 1477, 9760, 1995, 13, 9192, 369