{"id": "33", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "To cook pollock, first preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper and place them on the baking sheet. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which should take about 15 minutes. If desired, turn the oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet and return fish to the oven to allow cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nLook for specific cooking instructions or methods mentioned in the given passages for pollock.\nLook for details about the preparation or cooking method of pollock that are common to the given passages.\nLook for examples of how pollock is prepared and cooked in the given passages, including any specific techniques or ingredients mentioned.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 36.802, "generation_time_seconds": 25.5916, "selection_time_seconds": 11.2101, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3151, 17233, 1714, 9733, 476, 6131, 304, 279, 21085, 369, 1471, 1023, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.4162, -0.0014, -0.108, -1.9639, -0.2167, -1.0055, -1.4608, -4.0415, -0.1166, -0.0301, -0.001, -1.001, -0.671, -0.7222, -0.0, -0.0224, -0.0057], "cumulative_logprob": -12.784, "norm_logp": -0.752, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 17}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [10380, 369, 3151, 17233, 11221, 476, 5413, 9733, 304, 279, 2661, 46769, 369, 1471, 1023, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.8626, -0.0077, -1.2132, -0.0853, -1.2426, -0.0701, -0.9075, -1.1163,