{"id": "42", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to remove plastic from a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic, then scrape it off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. (Passage 1)\n2. Heat the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun to make it easier to peel off. Once heated, use a cloth to peel off the plastic. (Passage 2)\n3. Soak a cloth in an acetone-based nail polish remover and use it to scrub the remaining plastic off of the element after leaving it on the element for 5 minutes. Then, wipe the coils with a clean, damp cloth and remove any remaining residue with a cloth dipped in a solution of warm water and dish soap. (Passage 3)\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to remove plastic from the drum of a clothes dryer.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the type of plastic and its size to determine the appropriate method for removal.\nLook for any specific instructions or guidelines provided by the dryer manufacturer regarding the removal of foreign objects.\nLook for warning labels or care instructions on the dryer that may suggest how to remove plastic or other objects.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 47.31, "generation_time_seconds": 26.218, "selection_time_seconds": 21.092, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 11221, 3897, 304, 279, 46622, 594, 1196, 11376, 369, 3151, 18821, 389, 17592, 12188, 504, 279, 46622, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.4655, -0.0165, -0.0244, -3.8441, -0.5444, -0.5798, -0.0051, -1.9209, -0.1616, -0.7915, -0.0001, -0.