{"id": "60", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building a nest on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun.\n2. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it.\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds away.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to keep birds from building a nest on your porch is:\n\nAttach bird netting to the eaves or install bird netting over the light fixture, and/or mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch.", "pred": "To keep birds from building a nest on your porch, consider removing or replacing any items that could be used as nesting material, such as a bird feeder. Additionally, examine the surrounding environment for potential nesting materials or shelter, and consider sealing any gaps or openings that could allow birds to enter the porch.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: To keep birds from building a nest on your porch, consider removing or replacing any items that could be used as nesting material, such as a bird feeder. Additionally, examine the surrounding environment for potential nesting materials or shelter, and consider sealing any gaps or openings that could allow birds to enter the porch.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the physical characteristics of the porch such as open spaces, corners, and any objects that could be used as nesting material. Consider if there are any crevices or areas that might be accessible for nesting.\nExamine the surrounding environment such as trees, bushes, or overhanging branches that could provide additional nesting materials or shelter nearby. Consider any potential entry points for birds to the porch, such as gaps in the roof or walls, or openings near windows.\nIf the porch has open spaces, corners, or objects that could be used as nesting material, consider removing or replacing these items to discourage birds from nesting. For example, if there is a bird feeder on the porch, consider moving it to a different location or removing it altogether.\n\nAnswer: To keep birds from building a nest on your porch, consider removing or replacing any items that could be used as nesting material, such as a bird feeder. Additionally, examine the surrounding environment for potential nesting materials or shelter, and consider sealing any gaps or openings that could allow birds to enter the porch.", "time_sec": 70.758, "generation_time_seconds": 38.7279, "selection_time_seconds": 32.0302, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [37175, 279, 2701, 7354, 311, 2506, 19654, 504, 4752, 264, 22791, 389, 697, 44647, 1447], "logp_list": [-2.5075, -0.3336, -2.8023, -0.7127, -0.3208, -1.5961, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0401, -0.079, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0019, -0.0, -0.1152], "cumulative_logprob": -8.5097, "norm_logp": -0.5673, "input_len": 144, "output_tokens": 15}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [852, 7373, 5413, 504, 279, 46769, 311, 5358, 19654, 504, 4752, 95121, 389, 697, 44647, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-5.1861, -5.3371, -0.1119, -2.8627, -0.0038, -0.8609, -0.2731, -0.036, -0.0249, -0.0003, -1.8695, -0.0233, -0.0175, -1.4673, -0.0, -0.1252, -0.0072], "cumulative_logprob": -18.2068, "norm_logp": -1.071, "input_len": 144, "output_tokens": 17}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [3838, 5413, 476, 7375, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 4040, 19654, 504, 66710, 389, 279, 44647, 2041, 89155, 1105, 30, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.3111, -0.7508, -1.3772, -1.6995, -0.5973, -0.0193, -0.0017, -0.0011, -2.3284, -0.0031, -0.0013, -0.1054, -0.0112, -1.439, -0.0, -5.8604, -0.3035, -0.0216, -0.0686, -0.0011], "cumulative_logprob": -17.9016, "norm_logp": -0.8951, "input_len": 144, "output_tokens": 20}, {"