{"id": "197", "question": "leasing meaning", "gt": "Leasing refers to a process in which a firm obtains the use of fixed assets by making contractual, periodic, and tax-deductible payments to the owner of those assets. The lessee is the party receiving the services or assets under the lease contract, while the lessor is the owner of the assets.", "pred": "leasing is a financial transaction where a company or individual pays a monthly or annual fee to use an asset over a period of time, typically with the option to purchase it at the end of the lease term.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: leasing is a financial transaction where a company or individual pays a monthly or annual fee to use an asset over a period of time, typically with the option to purchase it at the end of the lease term.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nPassages mention leasing as a financial transaction where a company or individual pays a monthly or annual fee to use an asset over a period of time, typically with the option to purchase it at the end of the lease term. However, they do not provide a comprehensive definition or examples of leasing.\nThe given passages provide a basic description of leasing, explaining it as a financial arrangement where a party pays to use an asset over a specified period. The text indicates that this arrangement is typically for a lease term, suggesting the possibility of purchase at the end of that term.\n\nAnswer: leasing is a financial transaction where a company or individual pays a monthly or annual fee to use an asset over a period of time, typically with the option to purchase it at the end of the lease term.", "time_sec": 44.26, "generation_time_seconds": 34.084, "selection_time_seconds": 10.176, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [785, 21085, 3897, 1558, 537, 6644, 894, 