{"id": "223", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, to fix a lift valve in a toilet, you should follow these steps:\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain.\n3. Install a new flapper valve and chain.\n4. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n5. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n6. Push the solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and secure it tightly.\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm closest to the edge.\n8. Use pliers to securely fasten the chain.\n9. Turn the water valve back on.\n10. Test the flush of the toilet and adjust the chain if needed.\n\nNote: The given passages provide step-by-step instructions for fixing a lift valve in a toilet.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nI lack the information necessary to provide a detailed answer about fixing a lift valve in a toilet. The given question is too broad, and there are no detailed passages to guide the steps for fixing a lift valve.\nI will provide a general explanation of how to fix a lift valve in a toilet based on common issues and solutions.\nTo fix a lift valve in a toilet, begin by identifying the issue. Common problems include the lift valve not sealing properly, the float arm not functioning, or the fill valve not closing. Here are the steps to address each issue:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 57.328, "generation_time_seconds": 34.9498, "selection_time_seconds": 22.3777, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 11376, 476, 9705, 3897, 448, 279, 26214, 369