{"id": "381", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, first click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. Then, switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. Click on the Sort option. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. Alternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool to sort all worksheets.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the structure provided in the question, which states, \"how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical\". This indicates that we are looking for instructions on how to sort data in an Excel sheet alphabetically.\nIdentify the relevant information from the passage that pertains to arranging data alphabetically in an Excel sheet. Look for any specific instructions or examples provided regarding sorting techniques.\nExamine the passage for any instructions or examples on how to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically. Identify the specific steps or methods mentioned for sorting data alphabetically. Look for details such as sorting options, steps to follow, or any specific functions or features in Excel that can help achieve the desired sorting.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 44.876, "generation_time_seconds": 28.4355, "selection_time_seconds": 16.4405, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3250, 1141, 8, 311, 387, 10615, 27790, 2673, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.1127, -0.0028, -0.0085, -0.634, -2.5779, -0.0, -1.1986, -0.3231, -0.0518, -0.0459, -0.0, -0.1492, -0.0145], "cumulative_lo