{"id": "431", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "gt": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, first determine the extent of the tarnish. If the jewelry is slightly dull, filmy, or starting to discolor, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth into the solution. Rub the jewelry with the cloth, rinse in cool water, and buff with a cloth until dry. If the tarnish is heavier, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the jewelry and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth. If your silver jewelry is lightly tarnished, you can also try submerging it in a hot saltwater bath. Ensure that if your jewelry has gemstones, they won't be affected by the saltwater. For diamonds, clean with warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush, and pat dry with a soft cloth.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nSearch for \"How to clean tarnished jewelry at home\" on a search engine\nSelect a trusted website or article that provides detailed instructions for cleaning tarnished jewelry at home.\nRead the selected article or website for step-by-step instructions on cleaning tarnished jewelry at home.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 47.366, "generation_time_seconds": 23.5473, "selection_time_seconds": 23.8189, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [5890, 369, 330, 4340, 311, 4240, 86480, 3304, 30717, 518, 2114, 1, 389, 264, 2711, 4712, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.735, -0.365, -2.8872, -3.0956, -0.0071, -0.3704, -0.0265, -0.0011, -0.0261, -0.0411, -0.0001, -0.0471, -1.8469, -1.0598, -0.0397, -0.0, -1.6659], "cumulative_logprob": -15.2146, "norm_logp": -0.895, "input_len": 140, "output_tokens": 17}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0