{"id": "440", "question": "how are forest fires beneficial to conifers like jack pines?", "gt": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they help in the regeneration of the forest. Fires consume dead and decaying vegetation, clearing the way for new growth. Jack pines rely on fire to spread their seeds. They produce seratonous (resin-filled) cones that remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin, causing the cones to open and the seeds to fall or blow out. Furthermore, fires can disrupt the growth of other trees like spruce, providing an advantage to the more fire-tolerant jack pines and allowing them to proliferate.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify specific details or explanations in the given passages about how forest fires benefit jack pines.\nAnalyze the provided passages to find specific examples, numbers, or comparisons that illustrate how forest fires benefit conifers like jack pines.\nLook for sentences or paragraphs that discuss the positive effects of forest fires on jack pines or similar conifers.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 37.627, "generation_time_seconds": 26.9712, "selection_time_seconds": 10.6556, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [785, 3405, 17064, 911, 279, 7567, 315, 13638, 26084, 311, 390, 98813, 1075, 25072, 281, 1543, 13, 2014, 4226, 419, 11, 582, 1184, 311, 10542, 1995, 2878, 279, 46769, 429, 14758, 1246, 13638, 26084, 646, 387, 23699, 311, 390, 98813, 13, 1096, 4363, 17601, 279, 49853, 11364, 323, 76665, 315, 390, 98813, 311, 3940, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.7461, -0.8918, -0.0185, -0.1613, -0.1861, -0.0529, -0.0435, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0627, -0.0504, -0.0039, -0.1474, -0.0335, -0.0007, 0.0, -0.0851, -0.201,