{"id": "716", "question": "what exercises tone the chest", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, the following exercises are mentioned as toning the chest:\n\n* Modified tri-set for the chest (not specified)\n* Pushups\n* Dumbbell bench presses\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What exercises tone the chest?\" based on the given passages is:\n\nModified tri-set for the chest, pushups, and dumbbell bench presses.", "pred": "Exercises that tone the chest include push-ups, bench presses, and pull-ups. Push-ups primarily target the pectoral muscles, while bench presses engage the pectorals, triceps, and shoulders. Pull-ups, on the other hand, focus on the back and biceps but also work the chest muscles.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: Exercises that tone the chest include push-ups, bench presses, and pull-ups. Push-ups primarily target the pectoral muscles, while bench presses engage the pectorals, triceps, and shoulders. Pull-ups, on the other hand, focus on the back and biceps but also work the chest muscles.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nStep 1: Identify the specific muscles in the chest that can be toned through exercises.\nStep 2: Research various exercises that are known to target and tone the chest muscles.\nStep 3: Determine the most effective exercises for toning the chest based on their ability to engage the pectoral muscles.\nStep 4: Provide a list of exercises that specifically target and tone the chest muscles, including any variations or modifications.\nStep 5: Verify the information with credible sources or experts in fitness and anatomy.\nStep 6: Format the answer in a clear and concise manner, ensuring all relevant details are included.\nStep 1: Identify the specific muscles in the chest that can be toned through exercises.\nStep 2: Research various exercises that are known to target and tone the chest muscles.\n\nAnswer: Exercises that tone the chest include push-ups, bench presses, and pull-ups. Push-ups primarily target the pectoral muscles, while bench presses engage the pectorals, triceps, and shoulders. Pull-ups, on the other hand, focus on the back and biceps but also work the chest muscles.", "time_sec": 46.571, "generation_time_seconds": 28.1305, "selection_time_seconds": 18.4408, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-5.6101, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.006, -0.0], "cumulative_logprob": -5.6167, "norm_logp": -0.6241, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 9}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3151, 22932, 429, 2169, 279, 15138, 15747, 1874, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.1459, -0.008, -0.2761, -0.4277, -0.0637, -2.1098, -0.3842, -0.1415, -0.0002, -3.261, -0.1628, -0.1947, -0.0656], "cumulative_logprob": -8.2412, "norm_logp": -0.6339, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 13}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 1376, 6813, 315, 279, 3405, 624, 12, 576, 3405, 17064, 911, 22932, 429, 16232, 279, 15138, 382], "logp_list": [-2.9316, -0.0029, -0.0634, -0.0007, -0.0356, -0.099, -0.8552, -1.2946, -0.0095, -0.0264, -0.0021, -0.5431, -1.5189, -0.1212, -0.016, -0.1554, -0.0821, -0.0068, -0.0011, -0.0402, -0.0, -0.0, -1.1169], "cumulative_logprob": -8.9227, "norm_logp": -0.3879, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 23}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 3151, 23648, 304, 279, 15138, 429, 646, 387, 97731, 1526, 22932, 624, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 8319, 5257, 22932, 429, 525, 3881, 311, 2169, 323, 16232, 279, 15138, 23648, 624, 8304, 220, 18, 25, 29901, 279, 1429, 7373, 22932, 369, 8766, 287, 279, 15138, 3118, 389, 862, 5726, 311, 16579, 279, 281, 1256, 278, 23648, 624, 8304, 220, 19, 25, 39565, 264, 1140, 315, 22932, 429, 11689, 2169, 323, 16232, 279, 15138, 23648, 11, 2670, 89