{"id": "43", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to get plastic out of a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n4. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n\nIf the plastic is still difficult to remove, you can try heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun before attempting to scrape it off. However, if the plastic cannot be removed completely, it may be necessary to replace the drum or the entire dryer.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the type of plastic and its size to determine the appropriate method for removal.\nLook for any specific instructions or guidelines provided by the dryer manufacturer regarding the removal of foreign objects.\nLook for warning labels or care instructions on the dryer that may suggest how to remove plastic or other objects.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 47.498, "generation_time_seconds": 26.3505, "selection_time_seconds": 21.147, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 11221, 3897, 304, 279, 46622, 594, 1196, 11376, 369, 3151, 18821, 389, 17592, 12188, 504, 279, 46622, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.4655, -0.0165, -0.0244, -3.8441, -0.5444, -0.5798, -0.0051, -1.9209, -0.1616, -0.7915, -0.0001, -0.1662, -0.9248