{"id": "86", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "To prepare a blood slide, you will need a clean glass slide and a drop of blood. Place the slide on a flat surface and add a small drop of blood to one end of the slide. Take another clean slide and touch the blood with one end at a 45-degree angle so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly before placing them in slide transport containers.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the given passages for any step-by-step instructions on preparing a blood slide. Note any specific tools, techniques, or materials mentioned. Look for details on how to clean the slide, where to collect the blood sample, and how to spread the blood on the slide.\nLook for any specific tools or equipment mentioned in the passages that are necessary for preparing a blood slide, such as a microscope slide, a microhematocrit tube, or a blood collection device.\nLook for any specific steps or techniques mentioned in the passages on how to properly spread the blood on the slide for examination under a microscope.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 58.125, "generation_time_seconds": 36.0605, "selection_time_seconds": 22.0643, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 20772, 279, 6770, 7354, 369, 20045, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 2670, 87796, 323, 33639, 279, 6077, 389, 264, 8991, 14983, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.9414, -2.579, -0.1616, -2.3467, -0.3422, -2.5892, -0.0153, -0.0006, -0.0003, -0.3993, -0.4077, -0.3201, -4.2922, -0.6877, -0.8667, -3.5449, -2.3081, -4.683, -0.0827, -0.8919, -0.001, -0.0352,