{"id": "125", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the process of building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with compacted gravel, cutting and setting the 4 x 4 skids, cutting and assembling the floor with 2 x 6 rim joists and joists, anchoring the frame to the skids, attaching tongue-and-groove plywood flooring, constructing the walls separately, and raising them onto the frame.", "pred": "To build a lean-to shed, you will need a hammer, nails, a measuring tape, a saw, wood, and nails. The dimensions of the lean-to shed will depend on your needs, but a common size is 8 feet by 10 feet. To construct the frame, you will need to assemble the walls, floor, and roof using the lumber and plywood.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: To build a lean-to shed, you will need a hammer, nails, a measuring tape, a saw, wood, and nails. The dimensions of the lean-to shed will depend on your needs, but a common size is 8 feet by 10 feet. To construct the frame, you will need to assemble the walls, floor, and roof using the lumber and plywood.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the type of materials and tools needed for building a lean-to shed, such as a hammer, nails, a measuring tape, a saw, wood, and钉子.\nReasoning step 2: Determine the dimensions of the lean-to shed, including the height, length, and width, and the materials needed to achieve these dimensions, such as lumber and plywood.\nReasoning step 3: Describe the process of constructing the frame of the lean-to shed, including the assembly of the walls, floor, and roof, using the materials and tools mentioned.\n\nAnswer: To build a lean-to shed, you will need a hammer, nails, a measuring tape, a saw, wood, and nails. The dimensions of the lean-to shed will depend on your needs, but a common size is 8 feet by 10 feet. To construct the frame, you will need to assemble the walls, floor, and roof using the lumber and plywood.", "time_sec": 61.034, "generation_time_seconds": 33.6458, "selection_time_seconds": 27.3881, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [3838, 525, 279, 6770, 6813, 4362, 311, 1936, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 30, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.7995, -1.601, -0.0084, -0.6341, -1.6172, -0.9657, -0.1313, -0.1837, -0.0007, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0945, -0.0003], "cumulative_logprob": -8.0371, "norm_logp": -0.5741, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 14}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 7236, 4362, 369, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.3709, -0.0047, -0.0197, -0.3519, -0.1062, -0.0637, -0.343, -0.0559, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1848, -0.0106], "cumulative_logprob": -2.5116, "norm_logp": -0.1932, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 13}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 943, 315, 7236, 323, 7375, 4362, 369, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 23457, 11, 39843, 11, 264, 28990, 16971, 11, 264, 5485, 11, 7579, 11, 323, 107866, 44729, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.3709, -0.0047, -0.0197, -3.6555, -0.0398, -0.4416, -3.7295, -0.0068, -0.4682, -0.0588, -0.1216, -0.0278, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0, -2.5982, -0.4464, 0.0, -6.5147, -0.6746, -0.0002, -0.0033, -0.0047, -0.6614, -3.6857, -0.0, -0.0, -2.4053, -0.5927, -0.0005, -3.5896, -0.9873, -0.018, -6.2839, -0.0431, -0.2027, -0.0033], "cumulative_logprob": -38.6608, "norm_logp": -1.0449, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 37}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 7236, 2567, 369, 279, 15651, 4686, 24354, 8086, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.3709, -0.0047, -0.0197, -0.3519, -2.7847, -0.0706, -2.6742, -0.1993, -0.0, -0.0031, -1.4802, -0.0787, -0.0116], "cumulative_logprob": -9.0496, "norm_logp": -0.6961, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 13}, {"phase": "vote", "beam": null, "token_ids": [2082, 55856, 1817, 5754, 304, 7716, 1447, 24728,