{"id": "136", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "Sure! Here's how to roast individual garlic cloves based on the provided passages:\n\nTo roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of each clove, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\n5. Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n6. Season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices, if desired.\n7. Roast the garlic in the preheated oven for up to 45 minutes or until the cloves are softened to your liking.\n8. Store roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\n\nNote that the roasting time may vary depending on the size of your garlic cloves, so check on them periodically to avoid overcooking.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nBased on the question and the reasoning steps, the next logical reasoning step is to look for information about roasting individual garlic cloves in the provided passages.\nLook for specific instructions or methods mentioned in the passages for roasting individual garlic cloves.\nLook for specific instructions or methods mentioned in the passages for roasting individual garlic cloves.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 37.789, "generation_time_seconds": 23.5185, "selection_time_seconds": 14.2706, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 