{"id": "170", "question": "how to soften sugar", "gt": "To soften brown sugar, you can place it in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Then put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil and cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. To make hardened granulated sugar soft again, preheat an oven to its lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove the sugar from its package and put it in an ovenproof container. Place it in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon and if it starts to fall apart, turn the oven off and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the type of sugar to be softened (white, brown, etc.).\nIdentify the method used to soften sugar (e.g., soaking in water, microwave, or oven).\nDetermine if there are any specific tools or equipment required for the method chosen to soften the sugar.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 52.105, "generation_time_seconds": 25.8384, "selection_time_seconds": 26.266, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [27428, 279, 6961, 5888, 315, 13163, 311, 3535, 1128, 3643, 432, 2588, 323, 1246, 311, 79945, 432, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-4.8641, -0.6107, -1.5322, -0.0758, -0.0407, -0.0038, -1.862, -0.1784, -1.8721, -0.9045, -0.0116, -0.0138, -0.616, -0.074, -0.2931, -1.4922, -0.0001, -0.0333, -0.0334], "cumulative_logprob": -14.5118, "norm_logp": -0.7638, "input_len": 136, "output_tokens": 19}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [785, 3405, 330, 5158, 311, 79945, 13163, 1, 374, 10161, 369, 264, 1714, 476, 1882,