_tokens": 9}], "output_tokens": 830, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "183", "question": "how to cook a small prime rib roast in oven", "gt": "Before cooking the prime rib roast, let it stand at room temperature for at least 1 hour. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Season the roast with a small amount of salt and lots of fresh ground black pepper. Place the roast on a rack in a pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up. Roast it in the oven for 1 hour. After cooking, you can prepare au jus by placing the roasting pan on the stove over high heat. Add wine and cook for 8-10 minutes, stirring and scraping any brown bits. Add beef stock and cook to reduce the juice by half, which might take about 20 minutes. Add salt and pepper to taste.", "pred": "To cook a small prime rib roast in the oven, preheat the oven to a temperature between 325°F and 350°F (163°C to 177°C). Season the roast with salt, pepper, and other desired seasonings, and place it on a rack in a roasting pan. Cook the roast according to the desired doneness time, for example, a medium-rare roast might require about 15-20 minutes per pound at 325°F (163°C).", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: To cook a small prime rib roast in the oven, preheat the oven to a temperature between 325°F and 350°F (163°C to 177°C). Season the roast with salt, pepper, and other desired seasonings, and place it on a rack in a roasting pan. Cook the roast according to the desired doneness time, for example, a medium-rare roast might require about 15-20 minutes per pound at 325°F (163°C).", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nFirst, you need to preheat the oven to the correct temperature. This temperature depends on the desired doneness of the meat, but commonly, for a small prime rib roast, a temperature between 325°F and 350°F (163°C to 177°C) is suitable for a medium-rare to medium doneness.\nSecond, prepare the prime rib roast by removing the meat from the butcher's packaging. Ensure the roast is dry and season it with salt and pepper or any other desired seasonings. You can also use garlic, herbs, and other aromatics to enhance the flavor.\nThird, place the seasoned roast on a rack in a roasting pan. This helps the drippings collect at the bottom of the pan, preventing the roast from sitting in its own juices.\nFourth, place the roasting pan in the preheated oven and cook the prime rib roast according to the desired doneness time. For example, for a medium-rare roast, a small prime rib roast might require about 15-20 minutes per pound at 325°F (163°C), while a medium roast might require 20-25 minutes per pound at the same temperature.\nFifth,\n\nAnswer: To cook a small prime rib roast in the oven, preheat the oven to a temperature between 325°F and 350°F (163°C to 177°C). Season the roast with salt, pepper, and other desired seasonings, and place it on a rack in a roasting pan. Cook the roast according to the desired doneness time, for example, a medium-rare roast might require about 15-20 minutes per pound at 325°F (163°C).", "time_sec": 53.59, "generation_time_seconds": 42.6575, "selection_time_seconds": 10.9319, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3151, 1379, 315, 279, 10250, 20131, 57685, 9733, 304, 279, 3405, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.2728, -0.0019, -0.03, -1.3349, -3.1945, -0.7185, -0.0015, -0.5414, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.8065, -0.0389, -0.0001, -1.382, -0.0693, -0.0074], "cumulative_logprob": -9.4, "norm_logp": -0.5875, "input_len": 142, "output_tokens": 16}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 2661, 46769, 369, 894, 3151, 11221, 476, 17501, 369, 17233, 264, 2613, 10250, 20131, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.6299, -0.0164, -0.0147, -1.4084, -0.166, -0.0698, -0.327, -0.4506, -0.2007, -0.1037, -0.9575, -2.4529, -0.0041, -0.0005, -0.0333, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.1109, 0.0, -0.0244, -0.6919], "cumulative_logprob": -8.6638, "norm_l