{"id": "224", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Turn off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Fill the tank by turning on the water valve and then flushing the toilet. Adjust the lift chain as needed by moving the metal clip up or down a few links. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n5. Push the solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. Make sure it is securely fastened.\n6. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If it flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it tighter on the lift arm.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the type of toilet and the specific problem with the lift valve.\nDetermine the location and condition of the lift valve within the toilet tank.\nAnalyze the possible causes of the problem indicated by the lift valve's malfunction.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 54.487, "generation_time_seconds": 27.4476, "selection_time_seconds": 27.0394, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 3151, 943, 315, 11893, 31430, 304, 279, 26214, 11, 438, 2155, 4494, 1231, 614, 2155, 12733, 12538, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.3907, -0.0394, -0.0027, -4.5113, -0.7312, -0.3552, -0.2988, -0.0023, -1.0613, -0.0848, -0.0043, -1.6625, -0.0975, -0.1212, -0.7371, -0.0845, -1.502, -0.1555, -0.3562, -5.4638, -0.027, -0.0474], "cumulative_logprob": -18.7367, "norm_logp": -0.8517, "input_len": 139, "output_tokens": 22}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 