{"id": "338", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "To make ribs, start by removing the membrane from the bottom of the ribs with a knife. Place the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover them. Afterwards, line a baking pan with heavy duty foil. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer for heat circulation on all sides. Mix mustard and liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to make sure it adheres to the meat. To grill the ribs, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium and remove the ribs from the foil. Place them meaty-side up on the grill and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook for another 5 minutes. Continue this process until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through with grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the key ingredients and cooking methods mentioned for making ribs.\nIdentify the specific tools or equipment mentioned for preparing ribs.\nIdentify the specific techniques or cooking methods mentioned for preparing ribs.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 42.731, "generation_time_seconds": 23.5658, "selection_time_seconds": 19.1651, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [40, 686, 1349, 1526, 279, 2661, 21085, 323, 10542, 279, 9760, 7354, 323, 13966, 369, 3259, 55149, 11, 22573, 311, 2924, 3151, 10295, 11, 5109, 11, 476, 35495, 421, 807, 525, 3897, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-4.4341, -1.4273, -2.5264, -1.0723, -0.0032, -0.3936, -1.7905, -1.1277, -0.9714, -0.6157, -1.299, -3.208, -1.986, -0.93, -0.5384, -0.0073, -0.0001, -2.2749, -1.3765,