{"id": "35", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "To cook pollock, first, preheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Then, season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Next, place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes, or until the fish flakes easily. If desired, you can also add cheese on top of the pollock fillets and bake for an additional 3 minutes to melt the cheese.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nLook for specific cooking instructions or methods mentioned in the given passages for pollock.\nLook for details about the preparation or cooking method of pollock that are common to the given passages.\nLook for examples of how pollock is prepared and cooked in the given passages, including any specific techniques or ingredients mentioned.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 35.574, "generation_time_seconds": 24.5813, "selection_time_seconds": 10.9924, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3151, 17233, 1714, 9733, 476, 6131, 304, 279, 21085, 369, 1471, 1023, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.4162, -0.0014, -0.108, -1.9639, -0.2167, -1.0055, -1.4608, -4.0415, -0.1166, -0.0301, -0.001, -1.001, -0.671, -0.7222, -0.0, -0.0224, -0.0057], "cumulative_logprob": -12.784, "norm_logp": -0.752, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 17}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [10380, 369, 3151, 17233, 11221, 476, 5413, 9733, 304, 279, 2661, 46769, 369, 1471, 1023, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.8626, -0.0077, -1.2132, -0.0853, -1.2426, -0.0701, -0.9075, -1.1163, -0.0646, -0.0007, -1.9587, -0.0141, -1.0765, -1.0794, -0.0, -0.0113, -0.0169], "cumulative_logprob": -10.7275,