{"id": "88", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "Sure, I'd be happy to help you with that! Here are the steps to prepare a blood slide based on the provided passages:\n\n1. First, sterilize a needle with a flame as described in Passage 1.\n2. Next, obtain a blood sample by pricking your finger or using a blood donation kit. This will require adult supervision, especially if you are doing it yourself.\n3. Place a drop of blood towards one end of a clean glass slide as instructed in Passage 2.\n4. Take another clean slide and, holding it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide through capillary action. Gently push the blood along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Repeat this step to make two smears.\n5. Allow the smears to air dry completely before labeling them clearly and placing them in the provided slide transport containers as suggested in Passage 3.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the given passages for any step-by-step instructions on preparing a blood slide. Note any specific tools, techniques, or materials mentioned. Look for details on how to clean the slide, where to collect the blood sample, and how to spread the blood on the slide.\nLook for any specific tools or equipment mentioned in the passages that are necessary for preparing a blood slide, such as a microscope slide, a microhematocrit tube, or a blood collection device.\nLook for any specific steps or techniques mentioned in the passages on how to properly spread the blood on the slide for examination under a microscope.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 58.016, "generation_time_seconds": 36.493, "selection_time_seconds": 21.5232, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 20772, 279, 6770, 7354, 369, 20045, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 2670, 87796, 323, 33639, 279, 6077, 389, 264, 8991, 14983, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.9414, -2.579, -0.1616, -2.3467, -0.3422, -2.5892, -0.0153, -0.0006, -0.0003, -0.3993, -0.4077, -0.3201, -4.2922, -0.6877, -0.8667, -3.5449, -2.3081, -4.683, -0.0827, -0.8919, -0.001, -0.0352, -0.0066], "cumulative_logprob": -27.5034, "norm_logp": -1.1958, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 23}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 943, 315, 6543, 6077, 4362, 369, 279, 14983, 17975, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.6557, -0.0019, -0.0315, -1.6466, -0.0004, -0.0329, -0.8565, -0.4511, -0.3362, -0.0745, -0.1627, -0.1007, -0.079, -0.0061], "cumulative_logprob": -5.4358, "norm_logp": -0.3883, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 14}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 2661, 46769, 369, 894, 3019, 14319, 29208, 11221, 389, 20045, 264, 6543, 14983, 13, 7036, 894, 3151, 7375, 11, 12538, 11, 476, 7236, 9733, 13, 9192, 369, 3565, 389, 1246, 311, 4240, 279, 14983, 11, 1380, 311, 6530, 279, 6543, 6077, 11, 323, 1246, 311, 8865, 279, 6543, 389, 279, 14983, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.9414, -0.079, -0.0069, -0.8371, -0.0848, -0.1068, -0.2852, -4.6023, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0088, -1.4035, -0.1837, -0.0163, -0.0, -0.0048, -0.0622, -6.0598, -0.26, -0.0718, -0.5185, -0.1623, -0.452, -0.0002, -0.0018, -0.5996, -0.1328, -0.1938, -2.0783, -0.0001, -0.8523, -0.5072, -0.5378, -0.0942, -1.7642, -0.3772, -0.0495, -0.0021, -3.356, -0.0283, -1.0654, -0.1139, -0.0141, -0.2572, -0.0053, -0.2242, -0.0504, -0.0011, -0.3141, -0.4178, -0.1313, -0.85, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.047, -0.7209], "cumulative_logprob": -30.9358, "norm_logp": -0.5524, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 56}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 1376, 681