{"id": "107", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "The Windward and Leeward Islands are part of the Lesser Antilles of the Caribbean Sea. The Windward Islands are in the southeast and are exposed to the northeast trade winds, hence they receive more rain and are wetter. On the other hand, the Leeward Islands are located in the northwest and are away from the wind, making them drier.", "pred": "The difference between the leeward and windward islands lies in their exposure to wind and weather conditions. Windward islands are those that face the wind, typically receiving more rainfall and experiencing more turbulent weather conditions. Leeward islands, on the other hand, are located to the leeward (downwind) side and thus experience less rainfall and calmer weather conditions.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: The difference between the leeward and windward islands lies in their exposure to wind and weather conditions. Windward islands are those that face the wind, typically receiving more rainfall and experiencing more turbulent weather conditions. Leeward islands, on the other hand, are located to the leeward (downwind) side and thus experience less rainfall and calmer weather conditions.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nStep 1: Identify the types of islands being referred to in the question.\n- The question mentions \"leeward\" and \"windward\" islands, so we need to clarify what these terms mean in relation to islands.\nStep 2: Understand the geographical concept of windward and leeward islands.\n- Windward islands are those that face the wind, typically receiving more rainfall and experiencing more turbulent weather conditions.\n- Leeward islands are those located to the leeward (downwind) side and thus experience less rainfall and calmer weather conditions.\nStep 3: Compare the climate and weather conditions of the two types of islands.\n- Windward islands often have more humid and wet climates due to increased rainfall and cloud cover.\n- Leeward islands have drier climates with more sunny days and less humidity.\n\nAnswer: The difference between the leeward and windward islands lies in their exposure to wind and weather conditions. Windward islands are those that face the wind, typically receiving more rainfall and experiencing more turbulent weather conditions. Leeward islands, on the other hand, are located to the leeward (downwind) side and thus experience less rainfall and calmer weather conditions.", "time_sec": 66.549, "generation_time_seconds": 47.715, "selection_time_seconds": 18.8339, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 6961, 17452, 315, 279, 29000, 11, 1741, 438, 4268, 26331, 1379, 11, 52901, 4419, 11, 323, 9977, 4682, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.3885, -0.0164, -0.0082, -2.0211, -0.7411, -1.0093, -0.2055, -1.1765, -0.6593, -0.1084, 0.0, -3.1454, -1.0867, -0.7785, -0.1115, -2.9987, -0.5955, -0.0165, -0.014, -0.3548, -1.6483, -0.2298, -0.3589], "cumulative_logprob": -18.6729, "norm_logp": -0.8119, "input_len": 144, "output_tokens": 23}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 52901, 3728, 315, 279, 29000, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.3885, -0.0164, -0.0082, -0.414, -1.8069, -0.4773, -0.0667, -0.4004, -1.0857, -0.2448], "cumulative_logprob": -5.9089, "norm_logp": -0.5909, "input_len": 144, "output_tokens": 10}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 4494, 315, 29000, 1660, 13862, 311, 304, 279, 3405, 624, 12, 576, 3405, 33845, 330, 273, 24035, 1, 323, 330, 19154, 1606, 1, 29000, 11, 773, 582, 1184, 311, 37163, 1128, 1493, 3793, 3076, 304, 12687, 311, 29000, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.3528, -0.0023, -0.0501, -0.001, -0.1697, -0.0435, -3.4403, -0.0007, -0.0123, -2.3068, -0.8933, -0.0, -1.6045, -0.0123, -0.0052, -0.6566, -1.9532, -0.4526, -0.21