{"id": "137", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n6. Roast in the preheated oven for 45 minutes to an hour, or until the cloves are softened.\n7. Store roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\n\nYou can also season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices before roasting.", "pred": "Roast individual garlic cloves by preheating the oven to 375°F (190°C), placing the garlic cloves on a baking sheet or a pan, drizzling olive oil over them, sprinkling salt, roasting for 20-25 minutes, removing from the oven, letting them cool, peeling off the charred skin, and using them in your recipe.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: Roast individual garlic cloves by preheating the oven to 375°F (190°C), placing the garlic cloves on a baking sheet or a pan, drizzling olive oil over them, sprinkling salt, roasting for 20-25 minutes, removing from the oven, letting them cool, peeling off the charred skin, and using them in your recipe.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nWhat are the key ingredients and tools needed for roasting individual garlic cloves?\nThe reasoning steps are:\nWhat is the process for roasting individual garlic cloves?\n\nThe key ingredients and tools needed for roasting individual garlic cloves are garlic cloves, olive oil, salt, and a baking sheet or a pan.\n\nThe process for roasting individual garlic cloves involves the following steps:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 375°F (190°C).\n2. Place the garlic cloves on a baking sheet or a pan, with the cloves facing upwards.\n3. Drizzle olive oil over the garlic cloves, making sure they are well-coated.\n4. Sprinkle salt over the garlic cloves.\n5. Roast the garlic cloves in the preheated oven for about 20-25 minutes, or until the cloves are soft and the skin is slightly charred.\n6. Remove the garlic cloves from the oven and let them cool for a few minutes.\n7. Peel off the charred skin from the garlic cloves.\n8. Use the roasted garlic cloves as desired in your recipe.\n\nAnswer: Roast individual garlic cloves by preheating the oven to 375°F (190°C), placing the garlic cloves on a baking sheet or a pan, drizzling olive oil over them, sprinkling salt, roasting for 20-25 minutes, removing from the oven, letting them cool, peeling off the charred skin, and using them in your recipe.", "time_sec": 49.276, "generation_time_seconds": 31.134, "selection_time_seconds": 18.1415, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 3897, 46769, 369, 894, 2118, 11221, 476, 27787, 389, 926, 14725, 3842, 30635, 84288, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.069, -0.0471, -0.0169, -1.3664, -0.0581, -0.097, -0.2186, -3.2322, -0.0206, -0.0948, -2.2114, -0.182, -0.2533, 0.0, -0.0394, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0103, -0.4881], "cumulative_logprob": -9.4052, "norm_logp": -0.495, "input_len": 138, "output_tokens": 19}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [785, 3405, 17064, 1246, 311, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 13, 576, 3383, 7460, 41018, 279, 6961, 3565, 3019, 553, 3019, 311, 3410, 264, 15817, 16148, 315, 279, 926, 14725, 1882, 13, 5692, 374, 279, 1790, 19819, 32711, 3019, 1447], "logp_list": [-2.1404, -1.3377, -0.0495, -1.004, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1859, -1.644