{"id": "172", "question": "how to soften sugar", "gt": "To soften sugar, place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove damp paper towel in a couple of days. Alternatively, preheat oven to lowest temperature (150-200 degrees) and remove sugar from package. Put in an ovenproof container and place in the warm oven for 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon and if it starts to fall apart, turn oven off and leave sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the specific details or methods mentioned in the passages for softening sugar. Look for any techniques, tools, or substances that are suggested for this purpose.\nIdentify if the passages provide any specific methods or techniques for softening sugar, such as using heat, moisture, or specific tools. Look for any comparisons or examples given for the effectiveness of different methods.\nLook for any references to temperature or heating methods in the passages, as these can be effective ways to soften sugar. Check if the passages suggest using water or moisture to help soften the sugar.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 51.853, "generation_time_seconds": 31.621, "selection_time_seconds": 20.2315, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [22043, 429, 279, 3405, 17064, 911, 8413, 6019, 13163, 11, 582, 1184, 311, 10542, 279, 5413, 476, 12538, 429, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 11075, 419, 13, 45302, 11, 5413, 369, 8413, 6019, 13163, 21058, 7703, 1181, 31157, 2213, 476, 14