{"id": "295", "question": "what is the proper way to fertilize your grass", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass is to:\n\n1. Fertilize at the right time of year, which is at the beginning of the growing season, and varies for different types of grasses.\n2. Choose a fertilizer that is suitable for your type of grass and soil pH, as determined by a soil test.\n3. Apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern, avoiding over-fertilization, which can be determined by checking if the leaf blades bounce back up after being stepped on.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the specific components or methods of grass fertilization mentioned in the passages.\nExamine if there are any specific recommendations or guidelines on how often or which type of fertilizer to use based on the grass type mentioned in the passages.\nDetermine whether the passages describe any specific timing or application methods for fertilizing the grass, such as spring, summer, or fall applications, and how fertilizers should be applied (e.g., by hand, sprinkler, or spreader).\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 51.443, "generation_time_seconds": 28.3038, "selection_time_seconds": 23.1395, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 943, 315, 16359, 498, 614, 11, 438, 2155, 9419, 614, 2155, 49023, 8502, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.3388, -0.0014, -0.1265, -0.4869, -0.0096, -0.0444, -0.2259, -0.0189, -2.0313, -0.0095, -0.0752, -4.2867, -0.5196, -0.0951, -1.685, -0.2538, -0.0701, -0.0081], "cumulative_logprob": -11.2868, "norm_logp": -0.627, "input_len": 142, "output_tokens": 18}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 943, 315, 16359, 304,