{"id": "351", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Company goodwill is a business asset that is created when a business provides good service or product to their customers, leading to customer trust. This trust results in repeat customers and positive word-of-mouth, which can increase a company's customer base and retain old clients. Goodwill represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation of the business possesses. It is important because it can attract investors and future buyers, and it is an advantage of the reputation and connection with customers which tends to make that connection permanent.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the key aspects of company goodwill mentioned in the passages and explain its importance.\nAnalyze the specific examples or comparisons provided about company goodwill in the passages.\nLook for any explicit statements about the importance of company goodwill from the passages and summarize them.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 46.562, "generation_time_seconds": 23.4074, "selection_time_seconds": 23.1543, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 20772, 279, 7286, 315, 81646, 304, 264, 2813, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.8902, -1.113, -1.2924, -0.0864, -0.0029, -0.4828, -0.2482, -1.2297, -1.2515, -0.7483, -0.0041], "cumulative_logprob": -8.3495, "norm_logp": -0.759, "input_len": 139, "output_tokens": 11}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 1376, 3793, 1741, 438, 330, 10139, 81646, 1, 323, 3535, 862, 2266, 304, 279, 3405, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.533, -0.0028, -0.1429, -1.1753, -1.2041, -5.683, -0.0, -0.1356, -0.6946, -0.1064, -0.018, -0.0244, -1.