{"id": "423", "question": "what is a upc description", "gt": "A UPC description refers to the Universal Product Code, which is a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item and is mainly used for scanning items at the point of sale.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\n1. Identify the key terms: \"UPC\" and \"description\".\n2. Analyze the context or look for sentences directly relating to \"UPC\" or \"description\".\n3. Confirm if the passages provide enough details to describe what a \"UPC description\" refers to.\n4. Formulate the answer based on the provided information.\nExamine the passages closely for any mention of \"UPC\" or related terms that could help define or describe its purpose or function.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 43.211, "generation_time_seconds": 27.8238, "selection_time_seconds": 15.3871, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [785, 3405, 17064, 369, 264, 4008, 315, 264, 95129, 11, 892, 13352, 369, 25500, 5643, 6119, 13, 2014, 10277, 4226, 11, 358, 1184, 311, 3410, 264, 2797, 11, 63594, 7271, 429, 35616, 5961, 311, 279, 2661, 21085, 13, 8704, 279, 21085, 374, 537, 3897, 11, 358, 3278, 9245, 264, 4008, 3118, 389, 14260, 17473, 315, 95129, 82, 382], "logp_list": [-1.7632, -0.6318, -0.0782, -0.069, -0.1416, -0.1924, -0.0004, -0.5474, -0.03, -1.2221, -0.0224, -0.1437, -0.0, -0.0076, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0083, -0.4982, -4.8785, -0.0548, -1.838, -0.4714, -0.0781, -0.0078, -2.241, -0.9892, -1.392, -4.1947, -0.0291, -0.6034, -2.9389, -6.5462, -1.3831, -0.0003, -0.0673, -1.2786, -2.3472, -0.5158, -2.3481, -0.6301, -0.0879, -0.256, -0.0049, 