{"id": "433", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to clean tarnished jewelry at home:\n\n1. Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth to shine silver jewelry that is merely dull or starting to discolor. Rub the jewelry, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry.\n2. Use warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush to clean diamonds. Pat the jewelry dry with a soft cloth.\n3. Soak tarnished silver jewelry in a saltwater solution of two cups of hot water. This method is gentle and can remove tarnish without abrading the silver. Make sure the gemstones will not be affected by the solution before submerging them.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide information on how to clean other types of jewelry, such as gold or platinum, or what to do if the tarnish is heavy or if the jewelry has intricate designs that may be damaged during cleaning.", "pred": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, first identify the type of metal and finish of the jewelry. For example, if the jewelry is made of silver, you can use a mild detergent and a soft cloth to clean it. If the jewelry is made of gold, you may need a gentle cleaning solution. Gather your cleaning supplies, such as a mild detergent, a soft cloth, and a gentle cleaning solution if needed. Then, gently rub the jewelry with the soft cloth or a small brush, using the cleaning solution if necessary. Finally, rinse the jewelry with water and dry it with a soft cloth.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: To clean tarnished jewelry at home, first identify the type of metal and finish of the jewelry. For example, if the jewelry is made of silver, you can use a mild detergent and a soft cloth to clean it. If the jewelry is made of gold, you may need a gentle cleaning solution. Gather your cleaning supplies, such as a mild detergent, a soft cloth, and a gentle cleaning solution if needed. Then, gently rub the jewelry with the soft cloth or a small brush, using the cleaning solution if necessary. Finally, rinse the jewelry with water and dry it with a soft cloth.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the type of metal and finish of the jewelry.\nDetermine the appropriate cleaning method based on the type of metal and finish.\nGather cleaning supplies, such as a mild detergent, a soft cloth, and a gentle cleaning solution if needed.\n\nAnswer: To clean tarnished jewelry at home, first identify the type of metal and finish of the jewelry. For example, if the jewelry is made of silver, you can use a mild detergent and a soft cloth to clean it. If the jewelry is made of gold, you may need a gentle cleaning solution. Gather your cleaning supplies, such as a mild detergent, a soft cloth, and a gentle cleaning solution if needed. Then, gently rub the jewelry with the soft cloth or a small brush, using the cleaning solution if necessary. Finally, rinse the jewelry with water and dry it with a soft cloth.", "time_sec": 61.19, "generation_time_seconds": 30.8415, "selection_time_seconds": 30.3485, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 4240, 86480, 3304, 30717, 518, 2114, 11, 498, 646, 990, 264, 20980, 315, 27815, 38862, 323, 3015, 304, 264, 24937, 12681, 28137, 13, 20552, 419, 24937, 311, 279, 86480, 3304, 5671, 315, 279, 30717, 11, 1077, 432, 2444, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 11, 323, 1221, 73241, 448, 8205, 3015, 13, 30841, 279, 30717, 448, 264, 8413, 27292, 311, 5358, 3015, 18773, 13, 1752, 5107, 32405, 11, 498, 646, 990, 264, 6291, 315, 825, 949, 4158, 46105, 311, 2326, 5479, 3015, 311, 4623, 44029, 279, 30717, 13, 19881, 311, 5648, 1667, 24939, 25266, 476, 93704, 74865, 438, 807, 646, 5557, 279, 9317, 476, 18747, 32510, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.5743, -0.3338, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0028, 0.0