{"id": "666", "question": "what happens when you breath in and out", "gt": "When you breathe in, your diaphragm contracts and pulls downwards, expanding the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also contract to expand the ribcage. Pressure inside the chest is reduced, causing air to be sucked into the lungs. On the other hand, when you breathe out, your diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity, reducing the space in the chest cavity. Air rich in carbon dioxide is then forced out of the lungs and windpipe. Breathing out does not require any effort from your body unless you have a lung disease or are doing physical activity.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIn order to answer this question using the information from the given passages, I need to identify the relevant details about respiration.\nI am unable to provide a logical reasoning step since I have not been provided any passages to analyze. The given instruction states to answer the question using only the information from the given passages, but no passages have been included. Therefore, I cannot proceed with the analysis.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 43.171, "generation_time_seconds": 28.2829, "selection_time_seconds": 14.8881, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 23275, 11364, 6398, 304, 25938, 11, 2670, 76673, 367, 323, 505, 11866, 367, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.9142, -0.0047, -0.0201, -5.3923, -0.5563, -0.0638, -0.0074, -0.1787, -1.5076, -1.3518, -0.5323, 0.0, -0.0049, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.2687, -0.0086], "cumulative_logprob": -11.8114, "norm_logp": -0.6562, "input_len": 140, "output_tokens": 18}, {"phase"