{"id": "719", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "gt": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n\n1. Begin by bringing a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Gently slide an egg into your silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the egg's yolk.\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring that the pod stays upright and no water gets inside.\n4. Cover the pot with a tight-fitting lid and allow the egg to cook for 6 minutes.\n5. After 6 minutes, remove the lid from the pot and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to carefully lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the steps provided in the passage to understand the process of poaching an egg using a poachpod. Identify any specific instructions or tips mentioned.\nLook for any specific instructions or tips on using the poachpod for poaching an egg. Identify any details about preparing the poachpod, timing, or handling the egg.\nLook for specific details about how to prepare the poachpod and any instructions on handling the egg during the poaching process. Identify any tips on ensuring the egg is cooked properly in the poachpod.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 46.634, "generation_time_seconds": 25.9245, "selection_time_seconds": 20.709, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 1376, 7354, 6398, 304, 1667, 264, 3193, 610, 39073, 311, 3193, 610, 458, 18636, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.3143, -0.0016, -0.0102, -1.6821, -1.6853, -1.1035, -0.0, -0.7153, -0.008, -0.0179, -0.0001, -0.0009, -0.0657, -0.0002, -0.0