{"id": "36", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to cook pollock:\n\nPassage 1:\n\n* Spray a baking sheet with butter-flavored cooking spray.\n* Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n* Place the fillets on the baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n* Bake in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n\nPassage 2:\n\n* Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n* Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n* Bake the fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n\nPassage 3:\n\n* Bake the pollock fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n* Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on top of each fillet.\n* Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.\n\nTherefore, to cook pollock, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n2. Place the fillets on a baking sheet or in the oven.\n3. Cook the pollock until it flakes easily, either by baking it in the oven or on the stovetop.\n4. Add cheese to the pollock if desired and return it to the oven to melt the cheese.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nLook for any cooking instructions or methods related to pollock in the given passages.\nLook for specific cooking methods or preparations mentioned for pollock in the passages.\nLook for any examples or comparisons in the passages that demonstrate the preparation or cooking of pollock.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 46.464, "generation_time_seconds": 25.1913, "selection_t