{"id": "108", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind of the northeast trade winds and are located on the southeastern side of the Caribbean Sea. The Leeward Islands, on the other hand, are located on the northwestern side of the Lesser Antilles and are away from the wind. The windward side receives more rain and is wetter, while the leeward side is drier but still receives some rain.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe question asks for the difference between the leeward and windward islands. To answer this, we need to first understand what \"leeward\" and \"windward\" islands are.\nThe next logical reasoning step is to define what \"leeward\" and \"windward\" islands are and how they differ from each other.\nTo define \"leeward\" and \"windward\" islands, consider the direction of the prevailing winds and how it affects these island chains.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 55.787, "generation_time_seconds": 30.7409, "selection_time_seconds": 25.0463, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 6961, 17452, 323, 52901, 4419, 315, 2176, 279, 1967, 24035, 323, 22087, 1606, 29000, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.6564, -0.0028, -0.0837, -2.3632, -0.4475, -1.4455, -0.1667, -0.194, -0.0306, -1.4173, -0.0262, -1.1168, -0.0, -0.0564, -0.0036, -0.0, -0.1829, -0.1948, -0.0597], "cumulative_logprob": -9.4481, "norm_logp": -0.4973, "input_len": 144, "output_tokens": 19}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [785, 3405, 17064, 369, 279, 6672, 1948, 279, 512, 24035, 323, 9956, 1606, 29000, 13, 2014, 4226, 419, 11, 582, 1184, 311, 1156, 3535, 1128, 330, 273, 24035, 1, 323, 330, 19154, 1