{"id": "117", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "Based on the given passages, water shares can be transferred as follows:\n\n1. The current owner of the Water Stock Certificate must return the original certificate to the company and sign the back of the certificate.\n2. The new owner must provide proof of ownership and pay a fee of $75.00 to process the transfer.\n3. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\n\nPlease note that the passages only refer to the transfer of Water Stock Certificates and do not provide information on other types of water rights or transfers. Therefore, if the question is asking about other types of water rights or transfers, I would be unable to answer based on the given passages.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the specific process or method described in the passages for transferring water shares\nAnalyze the passage to find explicit instructions or descriptions of the steps involved in the transfer of water shares.\nExamine if the passage mentions any legal or regulatory requirements associated with the transfer of water shares, such as permits or licenses.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 54.434, "generation_time_seconds": 24.6934, "selection_time_seconds": 29.741, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3151, 1882, 476, 1714, 7481, 304, 279, 46769, 369, 49951, 3015, 13248, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.5228, -0.0011, -0.1618, -0.4171, -4.0879, -0.0534, -0.2457, -0.3713, -0.0283, -0.0001, -1.0286, -0.025, -0.0089, -0.0, -0.0003, -3.7941], "cumulative_logprob": -11.7464, "norm_logp": -0.7341, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 16}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840