{"id": "158", "question": "how to factory reset a htc one vx", "gt": "To factory reset an HTC One VX, you can follow the steps mentioned in passage 3. Slide the Notifications panel open, tap on Storage, then Factory data reset, and finally tap on Reset phone and Erase everything.", "pred": "After the factory reset is completed, you should follow any on-screen instructions to set up your device.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "After the factory reset is completed, you should follow any on-screen instructions to set up your device.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nTo factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n1. Power off the device by pressing and holding the power button.\n2. Use the volume button to navigate to the \"Settings\" menu.\n3. Scroll through the settings until you find \"Backup & reset.\"\n4. Tap on \"Backup & reset.\"\n5. Select \"Factory data reset.\"\n6. Confirm the reset by tapping \"Reset device.\"\n7. Wait for the process to complete.\n8. Once the reset is finished, follow any on-screen instructions to set up your device.\nThe reasoning steps are:\nAfter the factory reset is completed, what should you do next?\n\nAfter the factory reset is completed, you should follow any on-screen instructions to set up your device.", "time_sec": 59.712, "generation_time_seconds": 36.509, "selection_time_seconds": 23.2028, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [5890, 369, 264, 3151, 3772, 476, 8474, 304, 279, 11376, 476, 2860, 4963, 429, 11689, 33845, 279, 8633, 7585, 1882, 369, 279, 48267, 3776, 78177, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.1337, -0.2401, -2.2961, -1.269, -1.1172, -0.7169, -2.6746, -1.4965, -0.0013, -1.3942, -1.1995, -0.0577, -0.8823, -0.1381, -2.2884, -1.773, -0.545, -0.5556, -0.0023, -0.2001, -0.0002, -0.0672, -0.0, -0.0013, -0.0034, -0.0491, -0.1403], "cumulative_logprob": -21.2431, "norm_logp": -0.7868, "input_