{"id": "204", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "gt": "Chard, also known as Swiss chard, is a vegetable with large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It has a flavor that is stronger and more assertive than spinach, and some people find it bitter. Chard can be eaten raw in salads when it's young, but mature leaves and stalks are usually cooked or sautéed. Chard is actually a type of beet that is grown for its leaves rather than its root. It can produce white, yellow, or red leaf stalks. Chard is highly perishable and should be kept in the refrigerator for only 2 to 3 days.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nLook for a definition or description of chard in the given passages.\nLook for a detailed description of the appearance, texture, and possible uses of chard in the given passages.\nLook for any comparison to other vegetables in the given passages to provide context.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 48.525, "generation_time_seconds": 26.5768, "selection_time_seconds": 21.9477, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 2661, 21085, 369, 894, 6286, 315, 521, 567, 23880, 476, 5435, 1995, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.0182, -0.0333, -0.0059, -1.1759, -2.2555, -0.2373, -0.6052, -1.6467, -0.0791, -0.691, -0.0001, -2.9852, -1.9846, -0.8521, -1.4712, -0.0287, -0.0848], "cumulative_logprob": -16.1548, "norm_logp": -0.9503, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 17}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 6028, 17452, 315, 521, 567, 3118, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.4825, -0.0039, -0.1724, -5.8827, -0.0786, -0.1732, -0.2933, -0.0, -2.2221, -0.0, -0.0517, -0.3203, -0.177, -0.0328, -0.0206], "cumulative_