{"id": "304", "question": "what causes watermelons to explode", "gt": "Watermelons can explode due to external pressure, such as when a bunch of rubber bands are placed around the middle of the watermelon, causing potential energy to build up and eventually cause the watermelon to explode. Another cause of watermelon explosions is the buildup of gas inside the watermelon due to rotting. This increases the internal pressure and when the skin of the watermelon can no longer hold the gas inside, it will explode.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the potential causes of watermelon explosion, considering factors such as temperature, humidity, and the watermelon's internal structure.\nAnalyze the specific conditions or triggers that could lead to a watermelon suddenly bursting.\nConsider the effects of pressure increase inside the watermelon due to environmental conditions and how this might lead to an explosive release.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 45.41, "generation_time_seconds": 24.6738, "selection_time_seconds": 20.7357, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [19432, 279, 3897, 46769, 369, 894, 6286, 315, 9363, 429, 1410, 5240, 3015, 27127, 2382, 311, 15758, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.8078, -0.0099, -1.3637, -0.0982, -0.363, -0.0423, -0.7483, -0.0019, -0.5584, -0.2635, -0.3615, -0.3216, -0.0349, -0.0019, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0117, -0.3462, -0.7973], "cumulative_logprob": -9.1321, "norm_logp": -0.4806, "input_len": 139, "output_tokens": 19}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [40, 1184, 803, 2266, 476, 1995, 911, 279, 3015, 27127, 2382, 323, 279, 5240, 315, 279, 24199, 311, 3410, 458, 13382, 4226, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-4.79, -2.4259, -0.1697, -2.0109, -0.3888, -