{"id": "340", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make ribs:\n\nTo grill the ribs:\n\n1. Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium temperature (350°F to 450°F).\n2. Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\n3. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes.\n4. Flip and brush the ribs and cook for another 5 minutes.\n5. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\n\nTo prepare the ribs before grilling:\n\n1. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer.\n2. Season the ribs by mixing the mustard and liquid smoke (if using), and brushing the ribs on both sides.\n3. Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\n\nFor oven-cooked BBQ ribs:\n\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag.\n3. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover the ribs.\n4. Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil.\n5. Place the ribs in the baking pan and bake at 350°F for 2-3 hours, or until the ribs are tender and the meat starts to pull away from the bone.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the main ingredients for ribs, such as pork or beef ribs, and other essential ingredients like salt, pepper, and any preferred spices or sauces for flavoring.\nConsider the cooking methods available, such as grilling, baking, or slow-cooking, and determine which method best suits the type of ribs and desired texture.\nIdentify the specific preparation steps for each cooking method, including marinating the ribs, preheating the oven or grill, and the cooking time and temperature.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 48.984, "generation_time_seconds": 25.6819, "selection_time_seconds": 23.3022, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 3897, 46769, 311, 10542, 279, 2856, 7354, 476, 7375, 5871, 369, 20045, 55149, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.7555, -0.0474, -0.0071, -1.4345, -0.0284, -2.0991, -0.2529, -2.2454, -4.34, -0.4354, -0.2831, -5.7572, -3.4085, -0.1112, -1.5111, -0.0703, -0.0641, -0.2389], "cumulative_logprob": -24.0901, "norm_logp": -1.3383, "input_len": 136, "output_tokens": 18}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 13966, 4362, 369, 3259, 55149, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.2198, -0.0023, -0.0392, -2.2236, -0.7021, -0.0695, -0.0555, -0.0, -0.3353, -0.003], "cumulative_logprob": -4.6503, "norm_logp": -0.465, "input_len": 136, "output_tokens": 10}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 1887, 13966, 369, 55149, 11, 1741, 438, 35067, 476, 24317, 55149, 11, 323, 1008, 7565, 13966, 1075, 12021, 11, 24353, 11, 323, 894, 14890, 48559, 476, 89970, 369, 17172, 287, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.2198, -0.0023, -0.0392, -1.5986, -0.1338, -2.4765, -1.6811, -1.4715, -0.0983, 0.0, -0.408, -0.4698, -0.0006, -0.1513, -0.0981, -0.4518, -2.801, -2.2092, -1.4427, -0.1003, -0.8569, -0.0007, -0.0039, -0.0, -0.1287, -1.6008, -0.2995, -1.6331, -0.303, -2.3632, -3.9704, -0.316, -0.0962, -0.009, -0.0015], "cumulative_logprob": -28.4368, "norm_logp": -0.8125, "input_len": 136, "output_tokens": 35}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [2082, 55856, 279, 3151, 7354, 476, 5413, 7481, 304, 279, 46769, 369, 3259, 55149, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.8984, -0.0, -0.0095, -2.4803, -2.1295, -0.2957, -0.6381, -1.2184, -0.0239, -0.0005, -0.6146, -0.256, -0.2287, -0.0, -0.2097, -0.4028], "cumulative_logprob": -12.4061, "norm_logp": -0.7754, "input_len": 136, "output_tokens": 16}, {"phase": "vote", "beam": 