{"id": "384", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically:\n\nPassage 1 suggests using Kutools for Excel, which provides a Sort Sheets tool to easily sort all worksheets in alphabetical order. However, if you prefer not to use macros or Kutools, Passage 2 provides an alternative method using the built-in Sort feature in Excel.\n\nTo sort an Excel sheet alphabetically using the built-in Sort feature, follow these steps:\n\n1. Select the data you wish to sort by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu and select the column you wish to sort by (e.g., Product column in alphabetical order - A to Z).\n5. Click OK.\n\nOnce you have completed these steps, the data in your Excel sheet will be sorted alphabetically.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide sufficient information to clarify how to arrange an Excel sheet numerically.", "pred": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, use the Excel Sort function. Click on the column header you want to sort, go to the \"Data\" tab, click on the \"Sort\" button, select the column you want to sort by, and choose the sort order (ascending or descending).", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, use the Excel Sort function. Click on the column header you want to sort, go to the \"Data\" tab, click on the \"Sort\" button, select the column you want to sort by, and choose the sort order (ascending or descending).", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nTo arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you need to use the Excel Sort function. Here's how to do it step-by-step:\n1. Identify the column you want to sort alphabetically. You can do this by clicking on the column header that you want to sort.\n2. Go to the \"Data\" tab in the Excel Ribbon.\n3. In the \"Data\" tab, click on the \"Sort\" button.\n4. Excel will prompt you to choose the column by which you want to sort your data. Select the column you identified in step 1.\n5. Choose the sort order you want (ascending or descending). Excel will sort the entire sheet based on the column you selected.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nAnswer: To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, use the Excel Sort function. Click on the column header you want to sort, go to the \"Data\" tab, click on the \"Sort\" button, select the column you want to sort by, and choose the sort order (ascending or descending).", "time_sec": 47.273, "generation_time_seconds": 33.2929, "selection_time_seconds": 13.9805, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 498, 1184, 311, 990, 279, 21029, 15967, 729, 13, 5692, 594, 1246, 311, 653, 432, 3019, 14319, 29208, 1447], "logp_list": [-0.952, -0.2092, -0.0009, -0.008, -0.0001, -0.0025, -0.0, -0.0153, -0.7442, -0.9688, -0.0006, -1.7543, -0.0743, -4.1047, -1.6526, -0.305, -0.0504, -0.9989, -0.914, -0.2375, -1.2194, -0.0038, -0.0001, -1.2618, -1.7899, -0.0003, -0.0349], "cumulative_logprob": -17.3035, "norm_logp": -0.6409, "input_len": 139, "output_tokens": 27}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 1714, 311, 3378, 821, 304, 21029, 198, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 8427, 279, 821, 498, 1366, 311, 3378, 198, 8304, 220, 18, 25, 9189, 389, 279, 364, 1043, 6, 5651, 304, 279, 21029, 44567, 198, 8304, 220, 19, 25, 22201, 279, 364, 10231, 362, 311, 1863, 6, 2999, 1212, 279, 364, 10231, 609, 12339, 6, 1874, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.7377, -0.0042, -0.0242, -0.0009, -0.1897, -0.004, -2.6137, -0.8481, -0.5519, -0.4555, -0.7912, -0.0733, -2.1056, -0.6053, -0.0, -0.0, -