{"id": "411", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Push torn pieces of bread or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake in preheated oven until crumbs are dry but not toasted, 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs.\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\n\nIf you want to store the panko crumbs for later use, you can transfer them to an airtight container and keep them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nSearch through the passages for information about making panko crumbs.\nAnalyze the information found in the passages to determine the method for making panko crumbs.\nSince the question \"how to make panko crumbs\" is asked, the first logical step is to identify any information within the provided passages that describes the process of making panko crumbs. This involves carefully reading and analyzing the passages to find any explicit or implicit instructions or descriptions relevant to the process of making panko crumbs.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 41.571, "generation_time_seconds": 23.4005, "selection_time_seconds": 18.1704, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 2661, 46769, 369, 894, 3151, 11221, 476, 5413, 369, 3259, 281, 92852, 96577, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.6089, -0.1319, -0.0164, -0.824, -0.057, -0.1348, -0.0685, 