{"id": "489", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "You can see who liked your tweets by using tracking websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These sites can give you an idea of who is favouriting your tweets. Alternatively, you can also set up notifications on Twitter itself. By going to your account settings and clicking on the notifications link, you can arrange to be notified via email whenever someone likes one of your tweets.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the provided passages for any mention of features or tools that allow users to identify likes on tweets.\nIdentify specific details or examples provided in the passages that describe how users can determine if someone liked a tweet.\nLook for any mention of user interfaces or notifications that indicate when someone likes a tweet.\nAnalyze if the passages describe any changes in tweet visibility or any specific indicators that a tweet has been liked.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 50.448, "generation_time_seconds": 24.9718, "selection_time_seconds": 25.4761, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 4226, 279, 3405, 330, 4340, 646, 498, 3291, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 7521, 3118, 389, 279, 2661, 21085, 11, 582, 1184, 311, 23643, 279, 2500, 1995, 323, 8253, 421, 1052, 525, 894, 3151, 3565, 429, 3410, 18821, 389, 24588, 879, 14915, 279, 11809, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.9286, -1.6938, -0.1023, -0.0007, -0.1639, -0.9967, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.9261, -0.34, -0.0044, -0.0074, -0.0846, -1.2759, -0.0278, -0.5115, -0.028, -0.007, -1.6976, -0.0228, -2.6638, -0.0021, -0.9222, -0.9064, -0.0984, -0.5485, -0.6815, -0.056, -1.5385, -0.5867, -1.2096, -2.5023, -2.8985