{"id": "647", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to plant a potato that has sprouted:\n\n1. Cut the sprouted potato into chunks with two or three eyes each, making sure to not break the long sprouts.\n2. Allow the cut ends to dry out overnight in a cool, dark location.\n3. Plant the potato chunks or whole potatoes in well-draining soil, spacing them 24 to 36 inches apart.\n4. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep, and place the potato pieces in the bottom of the trench with the sprouted side facing up.\n5. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\n\nNote that the passages do not provide specific information on how to care for the potatoes after planting, such as watering and fertilization.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the given passage for any specific instructions or steps on how to plant a sprouted potato. If the passage provides detailed instructions, include those steps in your answer. If not, state that the passage does not contain enough information to answer the question.\nThe passage does not contain sufficient information to provide specific instructions on how to plant a sprouted potato.\nIdentify any general knowledge or common practices that are relevant to planting potatoes. Use this knowledge to create a general answer that does not rely on the specific passage.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 41.979, "generation_time_seconds": 28.906, "selection_time_seconds": 13.0734, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [37175, 279, 6770, 16170, 315, 38734, 47014, 323, 279, 3880, 315, 279, 38734, 8151, 411, 369, 6849, 6513, 1