": -0.0608, "input_len": 151, "output_tokens": 9}], "output_tokens": 409, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 8.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "667", "question": "what happens when you breath in and out", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are the answers to the question \"What happens when you breathe in and out?\":\n\nWhen you breathe in (inspiration):\n\n* The intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribcage.\n* The diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest.\n* Pressure inside the chest is lowered and air is sucked into the lungs.\n\nWhen you breathe out (exhalation):\n\n* Your diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity.\n* The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity.\n* Air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.\n\nTherefore, when you breathe in, the lungs take in oxygen-rich air, and when you breathe out, the lungs expel carbon dioxide-rich air.", "pred": "When you breathe in, the diaphragm contracts and moves downward, increasing the volume of the chest cavity. This decrease in pressure causes air to flow into the lungs. When you breathe out, the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward, decreasing the volume of the chest cavity. This increase in pressure forces air out of the lungs.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: When you breathe in, the diaphragm contracts and moves downward, increasing the volume of the chest cavity. This decrease in pressure causes air to flow into the lungs. When you breathe out, the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward, decreasing the volume of the chest cavity. This increase in pressure forces air out of the lungs.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the physiological processes involved in inhalation and exhalation.\nAnalyze the respiratory cycle, focusing on the movement of air and the change in the diaphragm.\nExamine the role of the diaphragm in the respiratory cycle during both inhalation and exhalation.\n\nAnswer: When you breathe in, the diaphragm contracts and moves downward, increasing the volume of the chest cavity. This decrease in pressure causes air to flow into the lungs. When you breathe out, the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward, decreasing the volume of the chest cavity. This increase in pressure forces air out of the lungs.", "time_sec": 55.8, "generation_time_seconds": 27.4942, "selection_time_seconds": 28.3053, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 52094, 11364, 6398, 304, 76673, 367, 323, 505, 11866, 367, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.7357, -0.017, -0.0063, -1.5631, -0.2119, -0.1673, -0.0085, -0.7554, 0.0, -0.0006, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.3543, -0.0434], "cumulative_logprob": -4.8635, "norm_logp": -0.3242, "input_len": 140, "output_tokens": 15}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [785, 3405, 17064, 1128, 8573, 979, 498, 36297, 304, 323, 700, 13, 20205, 389, 279, 2661, 2266, 11, 279, 19819, 1790, 3019, 374, 311, 23643, 279, 6961, 1882, 315, 25938, 304, 323, 700, 11, 892, 17601, 279, 7203, 315, 3720, 11, 279, 1853, 94796, 76, 11, 323, 279, 15138, 55329, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.1999, -0.4494, -0.0541, -2.3099, -0.0033, -0.0234, -0.0237, -0.0144, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.1722, -3.4452, -0.0, -0.0774, -0.5532, -4.396, -0.0471, -0.8419, -1.4563, -0.2739, -0.0029, -0.2743, -0.0042, -1.0329, -0.0404, -0.422, -0.8677, -0.1176, -0.1802, -2.2561, -0.0666, -0.002, -1.0306, -1.1888, -0.3238, -0.0183, -0.3519, -0.0039, -0.0699, -2.4171, -0.3152, -0.6938, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0255, -0.0087, -0.0351, -5.0305, -0.0449, -0.1003, -0.1945], "cumulative_logprob": -32.4617, "norm_logp": -0.6243, "input_len": 140, "output_tokens": 52}, {"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 1376, 13566, 315, 279, 3405, 25, 576, 3405, 17064, 911, 279, 1882, 315, 25938, 304, 323, 700, 11, 892, 17066, 1212, 279, 5582, 315, 592, 28479, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.9142, -0.0047, -0.0201, -1.2851, -