{"id": "695", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "To make ice cream, you start by stirring sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat just until the mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Next, transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mix thoroughly, for at least 2 hours. Once chilled, pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nRead the passage for instructions on making ice cream.\nLook for the specific steps or ingredients mentioned in the passage to understand how to make ice cream.\nIdentify the sequence of steps or the order of actions required to make ice cream according to the passage.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 38.22, "generation_time_seconds": 23.2874, "selection_time_seconds": 14.9322, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"phase": "rollout", "beam": 0, "token_ids": [785, 2661, 3405, 374, 330, 4340, 653, 498, 1281, 9853, 12644, 1189, 2014, 4226, 419, 3405, 11, 582, 1184, 311, 3410, 264, 3019, 14319, 29208, 1882, 369, 3259, 9853, 12644, 11, 3118, 389, 279, 1995, 2500, 304, 279, 2661, 46769, 382], "logp_list": [-1.7341, -1.152, -0.1539, -2.0124, -0.7043, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.7888, -0.4682, -0.0748, -0.0018, -0.6963, -0.3268, -0.2095, -0.0222, -0.0124, -1.8485, -0.0516, -0.3123, -0.0, -0.0, -0.7794, -0.4957, -0.0019, -0.0002,